hub.com/users/Riojaikumar","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Riojaikumar/Riojaikumar/commits/6151d0b6887dcaf8976f97393fc5795c4afbb97f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T21:16:42Z","email":"rohitjai7558@gmail.com","name":"Riojaikumar"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T21:16:42Z","email":"rohitjai7558@gmail.com","name":"Riojaikumar"},"message":"fix(profile): self-host the stats cards instead of a third-party service\n\nThe two github-readme-stats.vercel.app cards were rendering as broken images\non the live profile — the shared instance returns 503 DEPLOYMENT_PAUSED. That\nservice is frequently rate-limited or paused, so the profile''s only remaining\nthird-party runtime dependency was also its least reliable one.\n\nscripts/gen-stats.mjs now queries the GitHub GraphQL API and renders two\nself-contained animated SVG cards in the same palette as the hero and\narchitecture diagrams. No external service at render time.\n\nRows are drawn visible by default; motion (pulsing markers, language bars\ngrowing) is an enhancement only. An earlier draft animated rows in from\nopacity:0 and rendered a completely blank card whenever the animation did not\nrun — the same failure mode already fixed in hero.svg.\n\nConsolidates the snake workflow into one ''Build profile assets'' job so a single\npublish writes every asset to the output branch; two workflows targeting the\nsame branch would have clobbered each other. Adds a pre-publish check that\nrefuses to push a partial asset set.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016jscZ3HMrPhNPhUzFbry2K","tree":{"sha":"2afe98eaed98cd67a37d3154dc25d8e60ba05371","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Riojaikumar/Riojaikumar/git/trees/2afe98eaed98cd67a37d3154dc25d8e60ba05371"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Riojaikumar/Riojaikumar/git/commits/6151d0b6887dcaf8976f97393fc5795c4afbb97f","verificatio