lse,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/csp-editor/commit/7cc977ed8fcaa4d75e08e2907760b9f44f90943a","node_id":"C_kwDORwo7Z9oAKDdjYzk3N2VkOGZjYWE0ZDc1ZTA4ZTI5MDc3NjBiOWY0NGY5MDk0M2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/csp-editor/commit/0559a67c54fd99c5625028de9517912ef0f17638","sha":"0559a67c54fd99c5625028de9517912ef0f17638","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/csp-editor/commits/0559a67c54fd99c5625028de9517912ef0f17638"}],"sha":"7cc977ed8fcaa4d75e08e2907760b9f44f90943a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/csp-editor/commits/7cc977ed8fcaa4d75e08e2907760b9f44f90943a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/csp-editor/commits/0559a67c54fd99c5625028de9517912ef0f17638/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T07:28:10Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T07:28:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: raise coverage for csp-editor (SUPPORT-646) — Jest + Cypress, XSS-escaping and D1/D2 characterization tests (#3)\n\n* test: add pure-function characterization tests for highlightCsp (U6, U4, D2)\n\nTier 1 of SUPPORT-646 gap list: locks in today''s actual highlightCsp\nbehavior for three undocumented/divergent cases:\n- U6: an unterminated single-quote is silently dropped, not escaped\n- U4: wildcard highlighting only matches a bare ''*'', not ''*.example.com''\n- D2 (parts 2 & 3): csp-keyword has no allow-list, unlike csp-directive\n  (an arbitrary made-up quoted string and a typo of ''self'' both still\n  render as csp-keyword)\n\nThese are deliberate characterization/tripwire tests, not bug fixes.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: add component tests for readOnly CSS class, focus fallback, scroll-sync (U1, U2, F6)\n\nTier 2 of SUPPORT-646 gap list:\n- U1: assert the readOnly-mapped CSS class is applied/omitted on the textarea\n  (checkable via identity-obj-proxy even without real CSS reaching jsdom).\n- U2: the existing ''focus restore falls back to toolbar button...'' test never\n  actually broke ref.focus, so it only re-exercised the primary ref path\n  (confirmed misleading by Stage 4). Renamed it to reflect what it actually\n  tests, and added a genuine fallback-branch test that installs a one-shot\n  getter on the button''s .focus property (undefined on first read to fail the\n  primary typeof check, a spy-wrapped real focus on subsequent reads so the\n  toolbar querySelector fallback can succeed) to prove the else-branch\n  specifically ran. Verified meaningful by temporarily commenting out the\n  fallback branch in CspPolicyEditor.jsx and confirming this new test fails,\n  then restoring the source (git diff clean afterwards).\n- F6: scroll-sync half of the line-number gutter — forces textarea.scrollTop/\n  scrollLeft (jsdom has no layout engine) and asserts handleScroll propagates\n  them onto the line-numbers gutter and backdrop divs. Verified meaningful by\n  temporarily emptying handleScroll''s body and confirming this test fails,\n  then restoring the source.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: add init.js selectorType registration tests (F1)\n\nTier 3 item 7 of SUPPORT-646 gap list. New src/javascript/init.test.js\nmocks @jahia/ui-extender''s registry.add, stubs window.jahia.i18n.loadNamespaces\nbefore import (init.js''s module-level side effect), and uses\njest.isolateModules + dynamic require so the import-time side effect\nre-fires per test. Asserts:\n- window.jahia.i18n.loadNamespaces is called with ''csp-editor'' at import time\n- registerCspPolicyEditor() calls registry.add(''selectorType'', ''CspPolicyEditor'',\n  {cmp: CspPolicyEditor, supportMultiple: false}) with cmp referentially equal\n  to the actual component\n\nVerified meaningful by temporarily flipping supportMultiple to true in\ninit.js and confirming the new test fails, then restoring the source.\n\nNote: collectCoverageFrom in jest.config.js only scopes CspPolicyEditor.jsx,\nso this file''s coverage does not move the enforced 80% gate''s number (flagged\nseparately in the Stage 5 report, not fixed here per the gap list''s own\nscoping note).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: add real-i18next wiring test for CspPolicyEditor (F9)\n\nTier 3 item 8 of SUPPORT-646 gap list. New, separate\nCspPolicyEditor.i18n.test.jsx (deliberately NOT added to the existing\nCspPolicyEditor.test.jsx, whose module-level jest.mock(''react-i18next'')\nwould otherwise silently shadow this file''s real i18next import and make\nevery assertion pass against the mock instead of real locale data).\n\nInitializes a real i18next instance + I18nextProvider (no react-i18next\nmock) with the actual src/main/resources/javascript/locales/en.json bundle\nregistered under the csp-editor namespace, and asserts every t() call site\nin CspPolicyEditor.jsx resolves to en.json''s real content: aria-label,\nplaceholder, fullscreen/exitFullscreen button labels, fullscreen dialog\nheading, and the fullscreen hint text. Also asserts all 6 locale keys used\nby the component exist in en.json.\n\nCaught and fixed a real bug in my own first draft: the test resources were\nmissing the top-level ''label'' wrapper that en.json actually has, so every\nt() lookup was silently missing and falling back to the hardcoded JSX\ndefault — the exact vacuous-pass failure mode this test exists to prevent.\nVerified the fix is genuine by (a) a dedicated test that swaps in a custom\nresource string and asserts the render follows it, not the hardcoded\nfallback, and (b) manually editing en.json''s ariaLabel value and confirming\nthe render tracked the change, then reverting en.json (git diff clean\nafterwards).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: add SCSS and pom.xml source-contract tests (D1a, F11a)\n\nTier 4 of SUPPORT-646 gap list. Reads non-JS source files as text\n(fs.readFileSync) rather than through jsdom/component rendering, since\njest.config.js maps SCSS to identity-obj-proxy (no real CSS reaches jsdom):\n\n- D1(a): CspPolicyEditor.scss.contract.test.js extracts the .editorWrapper\n  rule block (brace-balanced substring) and locks today''s actual, documented-\n  divergent shape: min-height (not height/max-height) referencing\n  $editor-visible-lines, and overflow: hidden (not overflow/overflow-y:\n  auto). This is a deliberate tripwire for the D1 divergence (README says\n  ''10 lines, scrolls beyond that''; code grows unbounded) — not a bug fix.\n  Verified meaningful by temporarily rewriting the block to the\n  docs-matching shape (height + overflow-y: auto) and confirming 3 of 4\n  assertions fail, then reverting CspPolicyEditor.scss.\n- F11(a): pom.contract.test.js asserts pom.xml has no\n  <artifactId>content-security-policy</artifactId> dependency entry,\n  locking the ''no hard Maven/OSGi dependency'' documented claim.\n\nBoth are new test *shapes* for this repo but simple text/regex checks on\nsmall, stable files.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: add Cypress specs for site-level toggle, graceful degradation, rem sizing, unbounded height, forced-colors (F3, F11b, F10, D1b, U3)\n\nTier 5 of SUPPORT-646 gap list, items 11-15. New tests/cypress/e2e/02-cspPolicyEditor-gaps.cy.ts\n(kept separate from 01-cspPolicyEditor.cy.ts to avoid touching its existing\nsite fixture/logic):\n\n- F3: site-level ''Replace Content-Security-Policy at the site level'' toggle,\n  mirroring the existing page-level UI test but opening the site node''s own\n  edit form.\n- F11(b): graceful degradation when only csp-editor is enabled (own site\n  fixture, since the shared before() always enables both modules together)\n  — asserts the policy field/fieldset is simply absent, no crash.\n- F10: rem-based responsive sizing — doubles the root font-size and asserts\n  the editor''s computed font-size scales proportionally (tolerance band,\n  not exact equality).\n- D1(b): real-browser proof of the documented unbounded-height divergence —\n  types ~20 lines and asserts scrollHeight ~= clientHeight (no internal\n  scroll clipping) and .editorWrapper''s bounding-box height grows vs a\n  1-line baseline. Commented as a deliberate tripwire: if D1 is ever\n  resolved, these specific assertions must flip.\n- U3: forced-colors mode fully disables highlighting, emulated via\n  Cypress.automation(''remote:debugger:protocol'', Emulation.setEmulatedMedia).\n  Flagged in the gap list as the single highest-risk item (Chromium/CDP-only,\n  no cross-browser equivalent) — written to best current knowledge but NOT\n  exercised against a live browser this stage; explicitly flagged in code\n  comments and the Stage 5 report for Stage 6 to verify against the actual\n  CI browser image before trusting it.\n\nSTAGE 5 SCOPE: written, linted (0 errors) only — these require a live Jahia\nand the dockerized Cypress harness to actually run, which is Stage 6''s job.\nFull `tsc --noEmit` could not be run: tests/tsconfig.json has no\ncompilerOptions and pulls in a newer @types/node incompatible with the\npinned typescript@^4.4.4 devDependency (fails identically with this file\nabsent, confirmed pre-existing and unrelated to this change) — relied on\neslint''s @typescript-eslint parser (full AST parse, 0 errors) as the\navailable substitute automated check.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: fix genuine Cypress test bugs found by live Stage 6 execution run\n\nFour test-authoring bugs in 02-cspPolicyEditor-gaps.cy.ts were found and fixed\nafter running the full suite for real against a dockerized Jahia + Cypress\nstack (none are product bugs):\n\n1. F3 navigation bug: the ''site'' level case of openContentEditorAndRevealCsp''s\n   relativePath fallback landed on the site''s home page instead of the site\n   node itself (which has no entry in jContent''s Pages tree). Fixed by\n   fetching the site node''s uuid via GraphQL and navigating directly to\n   Content Editor''s uuid-addressed URL, verified live via a throwaway debug\n   spec before landing.\n2. F3 label-text bug: the site-level toggle''s real label is \"Add\n   Content-Security-Policy at the site level\", not \"Replace ... at the site\n   level\" like the page-level toggle (real content-security-policy-module\n   i18n asymmetry). Fixed to match the stable substring regardless of verb.\n3. D1(b)/U3 selector bug: [class*=\"editorWrapper\"]/[class*=\"backdrop\"] can\n   never match in a real browser - CspPolicyEditor.scss''s classes are true CSS\n   Modules and compile to opaque hashes, invisible to Jest''s identity-obj-proxy\n   mock. Fixed by locating elements via stable DOM relationships to the\n   textarea instead of hashed class names.\n4. U3 assertion bug: forced-colors hides the backdrop via display:none but\n   does not remove its highlighted spans from the DOM. Fixed\n   .should(''not.exist'') to .should(''not.be.visible'').\n\nFull suite verified green (9/9) via the real dockerized harness\n(ci.build.sh + docker compose run cypress against a provisioned Jahia\ncontainer), confirming the CDP forced-colors mechanism itself (04-gaps.md''s\nflagged highest-risk item) works reliably with no fallback needed.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"2f1049bf970453d7e1b71eb4ff1f4b65592f2122","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/csp-editor/git/trees/2f1049bf970453d7e1b71eb4ff1f4b65592f2122"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/csp-editor/git/commits/0559a67c54fd99c5625028de9517912ef0f17638","verification":{"payload":"tree 2f1049bf970453d7e1b71eb4ff1f4b65592f2122\nparent e25de2a72172ad07184e75982da500af5734497a\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1784100490 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784100490 +0200\n\ntest: raise coverage for csp-editor (SUPPORT-646) — Jest + Cypress, XSS-escaping and D1/D2 characterization tests (#3)\n\n* test: add pure-function characterization tests for highlightCsp (U6, U4, D2)\n\nTier 1 of SUPPORT-646 gap list: locks in today''s actual highlightCsp\nbehavior for three undocumented/divergent cases:\n- U6: an unterminated single-quote is silently dropped, not escaped\n- U4: wildcard highlighting only matches a bare ''*'', not ''*.example.com''\n- D2 (parts 2 & 3): csp-keyword has no allow-list, unlike csp-directive\n  (an arbitrary made-up quoted string and a typo of ''self'' both still\n  render as csp-keyword)\n\nThese are deliberate characterization/tripwire tests, not bug fixes.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: add component tests for readOnly CSS class, focus fallback, scroll-sync (U1, U2, F6)\n\nTier 2 of SUPPORT-646 gap list:\n- U1: assert the readOnly-mapped CSS class is applied/omitted on the textarea\n  (checkable via identity-obj-proxy even without real CSS reaching jsdom).\n- U2: the existing ''focus restore falls back to toolbar button...'' test never\n  actually broke ref.focus, so it only re-exercised the primary ref path\n  (confirmed misleading by Stage 4). Renamed it to reflect what it actually\n  tests, and added a genuine fallback-branch test that installs a one-shot\n  getter on the button''s .focus property (undefined on first read to fail the\n  primary typeof check, a spy-wrapped real focus on subsequent reads so the\n  toolbar querySelector fallback can succeed) to prove the else-branch\n  specifically ran. Verified meaningful by temporarily commenting out the\n  fallback branch in CspPolicyEditor.jsx and confirming this new test fails,\n  then restoring the source (git diff clean afterwards).\n- F6: scroll-sync half of the line-number gutter — forces textarea.scrollTop/\n  scrollLeft (jsdom has no layout engine) and asserts handleScroll propagates\n  them onto the line-numbers gutter and backdrop divs. Verified meaningful by\n  temporarily emptying handleScroll''s body and confirming this test fails,\n  then restoring the source.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: add init.js selectorType registration tests (F1)\n\nTier 3 item 7 of SUPPORT-646 gap list. New src/javascript/init.test.js\nmocks @jahia/ui-extender''s registry.add, stubs window.jahia.i18n.loadNamespaces\nbefore import (init.js''s module-level side effect), and uses\njest.isolateModules + dynamic require so the import-time side effect\nre-fires per test. Asserts:\n- window.jahia.i18n.loadNamespaces is called with ''csp-editor'' at import time\n- registerCspPolicyEditor() calls registry.add(''selectorType'', ''CspPolicyEditor'',\n  {cmp: CspPolicyEditor, supportMultiple: false}) with cmp referentially equal\n  to the actual component\n\nVerified meaningful by temporarily flipping supportMultiple to true in\ninit.js and confirming the new test fails, then restoring the source.\n\nNote: collectCoverageFrom in jest.config.js only scopes CspPolicyEditor.jsx,\nso this file''s coverage does not move the enforced 80% gate''s number (flagged\nseparately in the Stage 5 report, not fixed here per the gap list''s own\nscoping note).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: add real-i18next wiring test for CspPolicyEditor (F9)\n\nTier 3 item 8 of SUPPORT-646 gap list. New, separate\nCspPolicyEditor.i18n.test.jsx (deliberately NOT added to the existing\nCspPolicyEditor.test.jsx, whose module-level jest.mock(''react-i18next'')\nwould otherwise silently shadow this file''s real i18next import and make\nevery assertion pass against the mock instead of real locale data).\n\nInitializes a real i18next instance + I18nextProvider (no react-i18next\nmock) with the actual src/main/resources/javascript/locales/en.json bundle\nregistered under the csp-editor namespace, and asserts every t() call site\nin CspPolicyEditor.jsx resolves to en.json''s real content: aria-label,\nplaceholder, fullscreen/exitFullscreen button labels, fullscreen dialog\nheading, and the fullscreen hint text. Also asserts all 6 locale keys used\nby the component exist in en.json.\n\nCaught and fixed a real bug in my own first draft: the test resources were\nmissing the top-level ''label'' wrapper that en.json actually has, so every\nt() lookup was silently missing and falling back to the hardcoded JSX\ndefault — the exact vacuous-pass failure mode this test exists to prevent.\nVerified the fix is genuine by (a) a dedicated test that swaps in a custom\nresource string and asserts the render follows it, not the hardcoded\nfallback, and (b) manually editing en.json''s ariaLabel value and confirming\nthe render tracked the change, then reverting en.json (git diff clean\nafterwards).\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: add SCSS and pom.xml source-contract tests (D1a, F11a)\n\nTier 4 of SUPPORT-646 gap list. Reads non-JS source files as text\n(fs.readFileSync) rather than through jsdom/component rendering, since\njest.config.js maps SCSS to identity-obj-proxy (no real CSS reaches jsdom):\n\n- D1(a): CspPolicyEditor.scss.contract.test.js extracts the .editorWrapper\n  rule block (brace-balanced substring) and locks today''s actual, documented-\n  divergent shape: min-height (not height/max-height) referencing\n  $editor-visible-lines, and overflow: hidden (not overflow/overflow-y:\n  auto). This is a deliberate tripwire for the D1 divergence (README says\n  ''10 lines, scrolls beyond that''; code grows unbounded) — not a bug fix.\n  Verified meaningful by temporarily rewriting the block to the\n  docs-matching shape (height + overflow-y: auto) and confirming 3 of 4\n  assertions fail, then reverting CspPolicyEditor.scss.\n- F11(a): pom.contract.test.js asserts pom.xml has no\n  <artifactId>content-security-policy</artifactId> dependency entry,\n  locking the ''no hard Maven/OSGi dependency'' documented claim.\n\nBoth are new test *shapes* for this repo but simple text/regex checks on\nsmall, stable files.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: add Cypress specs for site-level toggle, graceful degradation, rem sizing, unbounded height, forced-colors (F3, F11b, F10, D1b, U3)\n\nTier 5 of SUPPORT-646 gap list, items 11-15. New tests/cypress/e2e/02-cspPolicyEditor-gaps.cy.ts\n(kept separate from 01-cspPolicyEditor.cy.ts to avoid touching its existing\nsite fixture/logic):\n\n- F3: site-level ''Replace Content-Security-Policy at the site level'' toggle,\n  mirroring the existing page-level UI test but opening the site node''s own\n  edit form.\n- F11(b): graceful degradation when only csp-editor is enabled (own site\n  fixture, since the shared before() always enables both modules together)\n  — asserts the policy field/fieldset is simply absent, no crash.\n- F10: rem-based responsive sizing — doubles the root font-size and asserts\n  the editor''s computed font-size scales proportionally (tolerance band,\n  not exact equality).\n- D1(b): real-browser proof of the documented unbounded-height divergence —\n  types ~20 lines and asserts scrollHeight ~= clientHeight (no internal\n  scroll clipping) and .editorWrapper''s bounding-box height grows vs a\n  1-line baseline. Commented as a deliberate tripwire: if D1 is ever\n  resolved, these specific assertions must flip.\n- U3: forced-colors mode fully disables highlighting, emulated via\n  Cypress.automation(''remote:debugger:protocol'', Emulation.setEmulatedMedia).\n  Flagged in the gap list as the single highest-risk item (Chromium/CDP-only,\n  no cross-browser equivalent) — written to best current knowledge but NOT\n  exercised against a live browser this stage; explicitly flagged in code\n  comments and the Stage 5 report for Stage 6 to verify against the actual\n  CI browser image before trusting it.\n\nSTAGE 5 SCOPE: written, linted (0 errors) only — these require a live Jahia\nand the dockerized Cypress harness to actually run, which is Stage 6''s job.\nFull `tsc --noEmit` could not be run: tests/tsconfig.json has no\ncompilerOptions and pulls in a newer @types/node incompatible with the\npinned typescript@^4.4.4 devDependency (fails identically with this file\nabsent, confirmed pre-existing and unrelated to this change) — relied on\neslint''s @typescript-eslint parser (full AST parse, 0 errors) as the\navailable substitute automated check.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: fix genuine Cypress test bugs found by live Stage 6 execution run\n\nFour test-authoring bugs in 02-cspPolicyEditor-gaps.cy.ts were found and fixed\nafter running the full suite for real against a dockerized Jahia + Cypress\nstack (none are product bugs):\n\n1. F3 navigation bug: the ''site'' level case of openContentEditorAndRevealCsp''s\n   relativePath fallback landed on the site''s home page instead of the site\n   node itself (which has no entry in jContent''s Pages tree). Fixed by\n   fetching the site node''s uuid via GraphQL and navigating directly to\n   Content Editor''s uuid-addressed URL, verified live via a throwaway debug\n   spec before landing.\n2. F3 label-text bug: the site-level toggle''s real label is \"Add\n   Content-Security-Policy at the site level\", not \"Replace ... at the site\n   level\" like the page-level toggle (real content-security-policy-module\n   i18n asymmetry). Fixed to match the stable substring regardless of verb.\n3. D1(b)/U3 selector bug: [class*=\"editorWrapper\"]/[class*=\"backdrop\"] can\n   never match in a real browser - CspPolicyEditor.scss''s classes are true CSS\n   Modules and compile to opaque hashes, invisible to Jest''s identity-obj-proxy\n   mock. Fixed by locating elements via stable DOM relationships to the\n   textarea instead of hashed class names.\n4. U3 assertion bug: forced-colors hides the backdrop via display:none but\n   does not remove its highlighted spans from the DOM. Fixed\n   .should(''not.exist'') to .should(''not.be.visible'').\n\nFull suite verified green (9/9) via the real dockerized harness\n(ci.build.sh + docker compose run cypress against a provisioned Jahia\ncontainer), confirming the CDP forced-colors mechanism itself (04-gaps.md''s\nflagged highest-risk item) works reliably with no fallback needed.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVzaLCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKn0QADNuZbcTXlj+gpTkuVhoXm+F\nbWpGix8GBglcZSsOSnYlOP0gTgrrlQ5Gfjf92Ik3ymYB81Kyz0X4MFTQCecnicyJ\niKH6k4YP593oOmPyxJZSQStAURY/HsWse3GL+VGvxfuxWtkzamoekcjDc6dW2o5W\n8O6DpBG4iGdNMpscf6gcVp3bVEZ9g5yd9mXCXbN/OF8zXFnxOi+xCEjX1Og08m3g\nF/k89C2E+6s/y2ic9XOtpAM2ncnwmsnfxQwSqVRa5mEG9If+OzypMMFRVdWy1mUE\n7EYklkYVTjXoc2NwziWcnUE93uZm1HSZR93qxBcyDyjZ9iaCau73ZNZZbpOKMJu3\n3UfWJ8vBzUzid3RMbyAlxpPuapTsipgm0n1j8z1ZjzVq2i1uJv5pXjCXD/CG4QT1\n5pZz6qj8GUiOtOwyrvVn5IDrVC76x9Cd1XM3URU6XZ2uujKjYZfQjwHSUeD9VAX0\nNyR592kZGQ4Ns4m3pScOJp4zN6b7rXhstGG8MTSCFiSJkYM1JYPYqr2D2Y+wWe39\nx1x5bcm5wFs0VNfVKXt8NdmeydLIyrDO2YfDqte6tuliiUsARvzUzQQcPoOlwSwV\nfd1kFCQnHYcXOKwmEwnYsezoTM4rhXBCD76XxdIZx8R1ZokOkakeZz9OAblvdh+K\nS4iqeLQ6HwCKVW/sjXQT\n=0Ppd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-15T07:28:11Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/csp-editor/commit/0559a67c54fd99c5625028de9517912ef0f17638","node_id":"C_kwDORwo7Z9oAKDA1NTlhNjdjNTRmZDk5YzU2MjUwMjhkZTk1MTc5MTJlZjBmMTc2Mzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/csp-editor/commit/e25de2a72172ad07184e75982da500af5734497a","sha":"e25de2a72172ad07184e75982da500af5734497a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/csp-editor/commits/e25de2a72172ad07184e75982da500af5734497a"}],"sha":"0559a67c54fd99c5625028de9517912ef0f17638","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/csp-editor/commits/0559a67c54fd99c5625028de9517912ef0f17638"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/csp-editor/commits/e25de2a72172ad07184e75982da500af5734497a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-19T10:50:16Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-19T10:50:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: harden CSP editor across quality, a11y, security, tests and docs (#2)\n\n* chore: harden CSP editor across quality, a11y, security, tests and docs\n\nOutcome of a multi-dimension review of the module.\n\nAccessibility (WCAG 2.2 AAA):\n- add accessible name (aria-label) and aria-readonly to the textarea\n- focus management + Tab focus-trap and role=dialog/aria-modal in fullscreen\n- visible :focus-within ring (replaces removed textarea outline)\n- AAA-contrast (>=7:1) syntax colours; readable base colour for unmatched tokens\n- forced-colors fallback (drops the transparent-overlay technique)\n- rem units + min-height for zoom/reflow; aria-hidden on icons; reduced-motion block\n- screen-reader Escape-to-exit hint\n\nSecurity / code quality:\n- escapeHtml now also escapes quotes; documented why dangerouslySetInnerHTML is safe\n- token regex made local (no shared stateful global); useMemo for derived values\n- prop-types + JSDoc; removed console.* statements\n\nInternationalisation:\n- wire useTranslation with English default fallbacks; complete en.json keys\n\nToolchain / tests:\n- root .eslintrc.json (extends @jahia) and .stylelintrc.json (stylelint 16)\n- jest + RTL setup (babel.config.js, jest.config.js/.setup.js)\n- 87 unit/component tests for the highlighter and component (>=80% coverage)\n- prune ~9 unused dependencies; production-safe default webpack mode\n- sonar.sources so the React source is actually analysed\n\nDocs: README accuracy fixes + Usage/Testing sections, CHANGELOG, CONTRIBUTING.\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address PR-review findings (accessibility + clarity)\n\n- make the placeholder visible (textarea color:transparent left ::placeholder\n  invisible) with an AAA-contrast colour\n- add a visible heading to the fullscreen dialog and label it via\n  aria-labelledby (WCAG 2.4.6 / 1.3.1)\n- restore focus robustly on fullscreen exit with a DOM fallback when the\n  moonstone Button does not forward its ref (WCAG 2.4.3)\n- also associate the Escape hint with the dialog container (WCAG 4.1.3)\n- aria-readonly as an explicit \"true\" string; drop redundant fixed height that\n  contradicted min-height on the editor wrapper\n- make the trailing U+00A0 sentinel explicit in tests; anchor jest\n  collectCoverageFrom with <rootDir>\n- README: describe init.js as the Module-Federation-exposed entry, not webpack''s\n\nLint clean, 94 jest tests pass (95.9% stmts), Cypress E2E still 4/4.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* refactor: resolve SonarQube findings on the React source\n\nSecond review loop, now that sonar.sources includes src/javascript:\n\n- replace the 34-complexity directive regex with a Set lookup (S5843)\n- escapeHtml uses a single regex + entity map instead of five chained\n  .replace() calls (S7781), keeping it compatible with the module''s\n  browser target (no String.replaceAll)\n- consolidate the fullscreen Tab focus-trap into the keydown effect and\n  drop the onKeyDown handler from the dialog container (S6848)\n- extract the textarea className to avoid a nested template literal (S4624)\n- tests: String.fromCodePoint over fromCharCode (S7758)\n- pom: classify *.test.jsx as sonar.tests so the repetitive test assertions\n  are not counted as production duplication\n\ntests: harden the Content Editor navigation against the transient loading\noverlay (z-index 9999) that can intercept clicks.\n\nLint clean, 94 jest tests pass, Cypress E2E 4/4.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* refactor: name the selectorType registration function (SonarQube S7726)\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"a4fa915df68c4dfff5ee4021a30f4d040228c468","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/csp-editor/git/trees/a4fa915df68c4dfff5ee4021a30f4d040228c468"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/csp-editor/git/commits/e25de2a72172ad07184e75982da500af5734497a","verification":{"payload":"tree a4fa915df68c4dfff5ee4021a30f4d040228c468\nparent 4d9da4c60e105651a1f6b50add1f11077d43baf4\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781866216 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781866216 +0200\n\nchore: harden CSP editor across quality, a11y, security, tests and docs (#2)\n\n* chore: harden CSP editor across quality, a11y, security, tests and docs\n\nOutcome of a multi-dimension review of the module.\n\nAccessibility (WCAG 2.2 AAA):\n- add accessible name (aria-label) and aria-readonly to the textarea\n- focus management + Tab focus-trap and role=dialog/aria-modal in fullscreen\n- visible :focus-within ring (replaces removed textarea outline)\n- AAA-contrast (>=7:1) syntax colours; readable base colour for unmatched tokens\n- forced-colors fallback (drops the transparent-overlay technique)\n- rem units + min-height for zoom/reflow; aria-hidden on icons; reduced-motion block\n- screen-reader Escape-to-exit hint\n\nSecurity / code quality:\n- escapeHtml now also escapes quotes; documented why dangerouslySetInnerHTML is safe\n- token regex made local (no shared stateful global); useMemo for derived values\n- prop-types + JSDoc; removed console.* statements\n\nInternationalisation:\n- wire useTranslation with English default fallbacks; complete en.json keys\n\nToolchain / tests:\n- root .eslintrc.json (extends @jahia) and .stylelintrc.json (stylelint 16)\n- jest + RTL setup (babel.config.js, jest.config.js/.setup.js)\n- 87 unit/component tests for the highlighter and component (>=80% coverage)\n- prune ~9 unused dependencies; production-safe default webpack mode\n- sonar.sources so the React source is actually analysed\n\nDocs: README accuracy fixes + Usage/Testing sections, CHANGELOG, CONTRIBUTING.\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* fix: address PR-review findings (accessibility + clarity)\n\n- make the placeholder visible (textarea color:transparent left ::placeholder\n  invisible) with an AAA-contrast colour\n- add a visible heading to the fullscreen dialog and label it via\n  aria-labelledby (WCAG 2.4.6 / 1.3.1)\n- restore focus robustly on fullscreen exit with a DOM fallback when the\n  moonstone Button does not forward its ref (WCAG 2.4.3)\n- also associate the Escape hint with the dialog container (WCAG 4.1.3)\n- aria-readonly as an explicit \"true\" string; drop redundant fixed height that\n  contradicted min-height on the editor wrapper\n- make the trailing U+00A0 sentinel explicit in tests; anchor jest\n  collectCoverageFrom with <rootDir>\n- README: describe init.js as the Module-Federation-exposed entry, not webpack''s\n\nLint clean, 94 jest tests pass (95.9% stmts), Cypress E2E still 4/4.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* refactor: resolve SonarQube findings on the React source\n\nSecond review loop, now that sonar.sources includes src/javascript:\n\n- replace the 34-complexity directive regex with a Set lookup (S5843)\n- escapeHtml uses a single regex + entity map instead of five chained\n  .replace() calls (S7781), keeping it compatible with the module''s\n  browser target (no String.replaceAll)\n- consolidate the fullscreen Tab focus-trap into the keydown effect and\n  drop the onKeyDown handler from the dialog container (S6848)\n- extract the textarea className to avoid a nested template literal (S4624)\n- tests: String.fromCodePoint over fromCharCode (S7758)\n- pom: classify *.test.jsx as sonar.tests so the repetitive test assertions\n  are not counted as production duplication\n\ntests: harden the Content Editor navigation against the transient loading\noverlay (z-index 9999) that can intercept clicks.\n\nLint clean, 94 jest tests pass, Cypress E2E 4/4.\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* refactor: name the selectorType registration function (SonarQube S7726)\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNR7oCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAiqAQAI39ouOcmhM9dOI3ErIRlPU9\n7n8fipKVzqXQXfgEW4Sm2WNUcR4OyGdrtPFiW8y2WQBds5W+gpfv92kCgUEoqqwE\nh2qkX1ZA/ynmJ+5ohU/t0VGPk3olfloRiOHqFrWjsYcW3xyNMJ7KHGIpLduLQ6ff\nOu1xz6dX+DhIx8YeyG4K81cXWmwt77qY70JOIUGOtJt3Y40A6z15ZY1SajSWzq76\nKW1rXLoSqDf0SfWtY+B1pKVuQVzIiSttA7ffUZWkdAW+WlvkD5ogAR4cCseaEXFU\nkEAMQTtdtpiWTtyM3PqxxOyH2FaajrxH0SL11pV5oJl3OYf9G7g9go3tNyPlVxNB\ntEWrMLKEv2dQefl/hz4cxpNAjopQ0TPKQyvEJNR45XJKxg44L2Izl2njen5BYFoa\nEHYd038zgV99hG6nzsvtfXAF1utsPIeEGe1Z/ae10doluKXwWoxbcHJGCrgAuMan\nP+9cwps6y/yXCY0kfmPl4APaHOvZMJ9ItPZ7qMSIuXVhx3qnTFHypNLxHg9u6aoc\nRTo1MaSy3Q+SOFGZiyH72/I0I7n6wmqdNceyEi8+afaxRKyrX2GbAnkOzisdDOYF\ndfp12OCUsisNiPiP1hLZQYl2KLh4ic7RzD7Ge8O1b/jDqdh3ZWVTWTL6EoP9B91A\nbQDZYH/423Zryee3b+rq\n=RQJc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-19T10:50:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/csp-editor/commit/e25de2a72172ad07184e75982da500af5734497a","node_id":"C_kwDORwo7Z9oAKGUyNWRlMmE3MjE3MmFkMDcxODRlNzU5ODJkYTUwMGFmNTczNDQ5N2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Jahia/csp-editor/commit/4d9da4c60e105651a1f6b50add1f11077d43baf4","sha":"4d9da4c60e105651a1f6b50add1f11077d43baf4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/csp-editor/commits/4d9da4c60e105651a1f6b50add1f11077d43baf4"}],"sha":"e25de2a72172ad07184e75982da500af5734497a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/csp-editor/commits/e25de2a72172ad07184e75982da500af5734497a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16238554?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/fbourasse","id":16238554,"login":"fbourasse","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjM4NTU0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fbourasse","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/csp-editor/commits/4d9da4c60e105651a1f6b50add1f11077d43baf4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-19T09:11:13Z","email":"fbourasse@jahia.com","name":"Florent BOURASSÉ"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-19T09:11:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"test: add Docker-based Cypress e2e tests for the CSP editor (#1)\n\n* test: add Docker-based Cypress e2e tests\n\nScaffold the tests/ harness (mirrored from securitytxt/tests) for the\ncsp-editor module:\n\n- docker-compose + Dockerfile + CI scripts (@jahia/cypress tooling)\n- provisioning installs Digitall and the content-security-policy companion\n  module (org.jahia.modules/content-security-policy:2.5.0), which supplies the\n  jmix:siteContentSecurityPolicy / jmix:pageContentSecurityPolicy mixins the\n  CspPolicyEditor binds to; csp-editor itself is deployed via MODULE_ID\n- 01-cspPolicyEditor.cy.ts: deterministic JCR data-contract checks plus a\n  Content Editor UI suite for the CspPolicyEditor selectorType\n- JCR fixtures: addMixin, setNodeProperty, getNodeProperty\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: drive CSP editor via created site + enabled modules\n\nRework the e2e spec around the real usage flow and verify it end-to-end\nagainst a licensed Jahia (4/4 passing, both locally and in the dockerized\nCI run):\n\n- before: createSite + enableModule(content-security-policy) AND\n  enableModule(csp-editor) — the jahia-content-editor-forms override only\n  enters a site''s form registry when the providing module is enabled on\n  the site, so both are required\n- selectorType wiring (API): assert forms.editForm reports the policy\n  field selectorType === CspPolicyEditor on the site and page nodes (the\n  exact value the Content Editor uses to choose the component)\n- policy persistence (API): round-trip a policy value via the jcr API,\n  adding the mixin explicitly (setCspPolicy)\n- CSP Policy Editor UI: open the Content Editor, expand Advanced mode +\n  Options, activate the page-level CSP toggle, and assert the custom\n  editor renders and highlights directives/keywords\n- provisioning: install content-security-policy 2.5.0 and the\n  dx-base-demo-templates template set; no site imported (the test creates\n  its own)\n\nFixtures: add getEditForm + setCspPolicy; drop addMixin + setNodeProperty.\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","tree":{"sha":"cec0f262c3214ebd60f16a96aa05bf9d0789b025","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/csp-editor/git/trees/cec0f262c3214ebd60f16a96aa05bf9d0789b025"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Jahia/csp-editor/git/commits/4d9da4c60e105651a1f6b50add1f11077d43baf4","verification":{"payload":"tree cec0f262c3214ebd60f16a96aa05bf9d0789b025\nparent 0aaee0ee8fc81bd43dac400860051db878dc5c9e\nauthor Florent BOURASSÉ <fbourasse@jahia.com> 1781860273 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781860273 +0200\n\ntest: add Docker-based Cypress e2e tests for the CSP editor (#1)\n\n* test: add Docker-based Cypress e2e tests\n\nScaffold the tests/ harness (mirrored from securitytxt/tests) for the\ncsp-editor module:\n\n- docker-compose + Dockerfile + CI scripts (@jahia/cypress tooling)\n- provisioning installs Digitall and the content-security-policy companion\n  module (org.jahia.modules/content-security-policy:2.5.0), which supplies the\n  jmix:siteContentSecurityPolicy / jmix:pageContentSecurityPolicy mixins the\n  CspPolicyEditor binds to; csp-editor itself is deployed via MODULE_ID\n- 01-cspPolicyEditor.cy.ts: deterministic JCR data-contract checks plus a\n  Content Editor UI suite for the CspPolicyEditor selectorType\n- JCR fixtures: addMixin, setNodeProperty, getNodeProperty\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n* test: drive CSP editor via created site + enabled modules\n\nRework the e2e spec around the real usage flow and verify it end-to-end\nagainst a licensed Jahia (4/4 passing, both locally and in the dockerized\nCI run):\n\n- before: createSite + enableModule(content-security-policy) AND\n  enableModule(csp-editor) — the jahia-content-editor-forms override only\n  enters a site''s form registry when the providing module is enabled on\n  the site, so both are required\n- selectorType wiring (API): assert forms.editForm reports the policy\n  field selectorType === CspPolicyEditor on the site and page nodes (the\n  exact value the Content Editor uses to choose the component)\n- policy persistence (API): round-trip a policy value via the jcr API,\n  adding the mixin explicitly (setCspPolicy)\n- CSP Policy Editor UI: open the Content Editor, expand Advanced mode +\n  Options, activate the page-level CSP toggle, and assert the custom\n  editor renders and highlights directives/keywords\n- provisioning: install content-security-policy 2.5.0 and the\n  dx-base-demo-templates template set; no site imported (the test creates\n  its own)\n\nFixtures: add getEditForm + setCspPolicy; drop addMixin + setNodeProperty.\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>\n\n---------\n\nSigned-off-by: Florent BOURASSE <fbourasse@jahia.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNQexCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALTYQAH5QKIBCHT98KNUpMRRg7v8v\nTLvvPyMIBIu90TepJP/Q6axbROVajdp65wdeGIOV2A6ryd3FmihejiBpQbm2IA+u\nxYjvpVTR5zGW6Bjd0jHh/RjIeiRGZ8I2v1IQv/0gC2SAfeDH90KCjaIfxQnNW0eT\nwLB9w3/M/LcoPyWNBH6XBZC+9v6gantBLsFN8KDHrnYAQZ66OC+AUxT4GrvfPuAd\nvPHyL+qsqlW0QJlVGGr2/2hCf7ERo7oGHxN4oSGbGNJ1x+1NssIJjIBquAt4yl+1\nvnzxtnWaIbF28HGyE0jJtfYTYC+BdgunQTpbpLLDSNZwuawz7t5pMWCf2yy715M7\nPfaJaYxGgdA67lIg7zk4CvCrBjSIMY2PB826EIA3luEKOwFAMjdab1yeOhnadUnp\nlYQShIOujo7yMDf+RRjMKIlF7/WrE7+NS5pxJl2sh2Fpia2QCDs7VAog6lVjHdDi\nnJtQAgk5XIit82Hi/0cB7BAqIAeIqxAKIZvwqffxskbZ+VQWuAYhOn0U7DCXFvXL\nsycxf/+9hkHEcGm3EAUjMebdqYIVeiSDc/qkADZdDEY+e/kU11HsCVNl2xZHg2rz\nFmqv8P3uOzeAHo3F7Gt6MlULm4u3D6bOWsGgy+O7gL0UzZQ+w05wHEhgXHuHPd06\nWyPI5Bk1NpNgm73080s/\n=CDP6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-19T09:11:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar