epos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commit/63d2c48c474f11b6d946fd794d57030e21ad32eb","node_id":"C_kwDORwxuadoAKDYzZDJjNDhjNDc0ZjExYjZkOTQ2ZmQ3OTRkNTcwMzBlMjFhZDMyZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commit/d1693101661b7ec5b83157a089c8b5a8f029c13d","sha":"d1693101661b7ec5b83157a089c8b5a8f029c13d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/d1693101661b7ec5b83157a089c8b5a8f029c13d"}],"sha":"63d2c48c474f11b6d946fd794d57030e21ad32eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/63d2c48c474f11b6d946fd794d57030e21ad32eb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13999850?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce","id":13999850,"login":"davidarce","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTk5ODUw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/d1693101661b7ec5b83157a089c8b5a8f029c13d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T17:54:29Z","email":"davidarce2915@gmail.com","name":"David Arce"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T17:54:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(workflows/sdd): add strict state.yaml directive to Claude variant + cleanup AskUserQuestion mention (#69)\n\n* fix(workflows/sdd): add strict state.yaml directive to Claude variant + drop AskUserQuestion mention from OpenCode\n\nTwo small follow-ups from the post-merge verification of PR #67:\n\n1. ORCHESTRATOR.claude.md was missed in the strict-directive rollout.\n   PR #67 added the \"Write state.yaml STRICTLY...do not invent fields\"\n   directive to ORCHESTRATOR.{md,opencode.md,copilot.md} but not to the\n   Claude variant. The Claude renderer prefers the .claude.md variant\n   when present, so the generic ORCHESTRATOR.md change had no effect\n   for Claude installs. This commit copies the same directive into\n   the Claude variant Post-Phase Step 2.\n\n2. ORCHESTRATOR.opencode.md L58 had a cosmetic mention of\n   \"AskUserQuestion-equivalent prompts\" alongside `question`. That\n   wording leaked the Claude tool name into the OpenCode prompt. The\n   OpenCode orchestrator only has `question` available; mentioning\n   AskUserQuestion adds noise without value. Trimmed to just `question`.\n\n* fix(workflows/sdd): drop AskUserQuestion mention from OpenCode bash-echo guard\n\nFollow-up to the previous commit. ORCHESTRATOR.opencode.md L58 had a\ncosmetic mention of \"AskUserQuestion-equivalent prompts\" alongside\n`question`. That wording leaked the Claude tool name into the OpenCode\nprompt where only `question` is available; mentioning AskUserQuestion\nadds noise without value. Trimmed to just `question`.\n\nThe previous commit''s body advertised this change but the actual edit\nlanded in this commit instead — the amend that combined them got\nblocked by safety rules.","tree":{"sha":"2893cd1c0837f137f5139e32b1cfc5912a3c4e59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/trees/2893cd1c0837f137f5139e32b1cfc5912a3c4e59"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/commits/d1693101661b7ec5b83157a089c8b5a8f029c13d","verification":{"payload":"tree 2893cd1c0837f137f5139e32b1cfc5912a3c4e59\nparent b237b6f0d46150ef63dfdd2eb1630bf97d596eba\nauthor David Arce <davidarce2915@gmail.com> 1778435669 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778435669 +0200\n\nfix(workflows/sdd): add strict state.yaml directive to Claude variant + cleanup AskUserQuestion mention (#69)\n\n* fix(workflows/sdd): add strict state.yaml directive to Claude variant + drop AskUserQuestion mention from OpenCode\n\nTwo small follow-ups from the post-merge verification of PR #67:\n\n1. ORCHESTRATOR.claude.md was missed in the strict-directive rollout.\n   PR #67 added the \"Write state.yaml STRICTLY...do not invent fields\"\n   directive to ORCHESTRATOR.{md,opencode.md,copilot.md} but not to the\n   Claude variant. The Claude renderer prefers the .claude.md variant\n   when present, so the generic ORCHESTRATOR.md change had no effect\n   for Claude installs. This commit copies the same directive into\n   the Claude variant Post-Phase Step 2.\n\n2. ORCHESTRATOR.opencode.md L58 had a cosmetic mention of\n   \"AskUserQuestion-equivalent prompts\" alongside `question`. That\n   wording leaked the Claude tool name into the OpenCode prompt. The\n   OpenCode orchestrator only has `question` available; mentioning\n   AskUserQuestion adds noise without value. Trimmed to just `question`.\n\n* fix(workflows/sdd): drop AskUserQuestion mention from OpenCode bash-echo guard\n\nFollow-up to the previous commit. ORCHESTRATOR.opencode.md L58 had a\ncosmetic mention of \"AskUserQuestion-equivalent prompts\" alongside\n`question`. That wording leaked the Claude tool name into the OpenCode\nprompt where only `question` is available; mentioning AskUserQuestion\nadds noise without value. Trimmed to just `question`.\n\nThe previous commit''s body advertised this change but the actual edit\nlanded in this commit instead — the amend that combined them got\nblocked by safety rules.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAMZVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALTAQAHHLEN3d57Z1uoYDnReLBrgn\n1yTBFzIsaXmRTuzsYb+w+4LuxRxlbMEKNCZpQJIFf27ahqNFBfzd2J0kuxkoHofw\n6p5FvI67RjSND8BlOdLjlFqw2+hyMUtjqs26QlcZZOl1ABH7dQTMLxlL1i5IsgCS\nXc4lMPvs2P40YR/cykd1Fj2/OUhPvoOD+hpXK0ihi8YxM7aKgj1nO7aaKa8WTu8D\nR3Uj13IeFDtObDV7F4bD1VbuV/GEpw4RSmtkQGCBWn4I4Eyy+72YRyEzVTLXkccd\n5X+MU4PkfMadVJZxyvpoJ2QjIsoZznK2uAcp+UvyJJNy3sWJ1x767lubpBenJZqI\noWmxIfZ7BXO2vkuo/cfZCnL1/PSNsztXYjsX0B8wNR/nVPpDTegRgB7XGRvwVucK\nmJZ5o7QQT6ArsJF1NdKeyXMy8c7cDWw1lvFCkmn4sqx1mi6SD2cvHqIOVtNSuEeP\nThMi1YZB4mS7iT02mLt5X8QDwm5ROkgsCSmPglVMl7gH33Th1DLF2e7wXh0R315d\n22ATuqP2gOa2PFI4hbTUk2VgaBu74SAvw2QuYGKt0iSBcW0o67NanGd0vlppmqhM\ngVhjgww3HJp05VndNcT11wBBj3jRIavOk90389C4kA7YdbWBokRY/tuFKS449chu\nSfUgH/MM6v9pXjmZM08g\n=Pe23\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-10T17:54:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscr