-05-10T17:32:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commit/b237b6f0d46150ef63dfdd2eb1630bf97d596eba","node_id":"C_kwDORwxuadoAKGIyMzdiNmYwZDQ2MTUwZWY2M2RmZGQyZWIxNjMwYmY5N2Q1OTZlYmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commit/a63883bad44136e9407d45c6f74f704e2149224d","sha":"a63883bad44136e9407d45c6f74f704e2149224d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/a63883bad44136e9407d45c6f74f704e2149224d"}],"sha":"b237b6f0d46150ef63dfdd2eb1630bf97d596eba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/b237b6f0d46150ef63dfdd2eb1630bf97d596eba"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13999850?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce","id":13999850,"login":"davidarce","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTk5ODUw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/a63883bad44136e9407d45c6f74f704e2149224d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T17:31:59Z","email":"davidarce2915@gmail.com","name":"David Arce"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T17:31:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(workflows/sdd): compaction hook + persistence-contract enforcement (#67)\n\n* fix(workflows/sdd): align persistence-contract with canonical state.yaml schema + enforce\n\nThe orchestrator (Opus 4.7 in session-ses_1ed8.md) wrote a state.yaml\nthat diverged significantly from the documented contract:\n- Field names differed (`phase` vs `current_phase`, `next` vs\n  `last_envelope.next_recommended`, `phase_status` vs `status`).\n- Extra fields were invented (`project`, `branch`, `engram:` map,\n  `risks:`, `gates:`, `notes:`, `implement:`, `created`, `updated`).\n- One field was an outright contract violation: `artifacts:` is\n  documented as \"Explicitly NOT in state.yaml\" but was written anyway.\n\nThe contract was unenforceable because the schema was loose and the\norchestrator instructions only said \"per schema\" without \"STRICTLY\".\nResult: the OpenCode compaction hook (which parses by exact field\nnames) reported `Current phase: unknown / NEXT: check state.yaml`\nbecause its regexes did not match what the orchestrator actually wrote.\n\nThis change:\n\n- Adopts the orchestrator''s natural canonical names as the documented\n  schema (`phase`, `phase_status`, `next`) — they are simpler and the\n  contract now matches reality.\n- Allows the useful additions Opus invented as OPTIONAL fields:\n  `project`, `branch`, `engram:` map. These help cross-session recovery\n  without bloating state.\n- Explicitly forbids fields that duplicate information available\n  elsewhere: `artifacts:` (filesystem), `gates:` (envelope), `risks:`\n  (plan.md), `notes:`, `implement:` (derivable from `[X]` markers in\n  plan.md), `created`/`updated` (use `last_updated` ISO 8601).\n- Adds a \"Schema Enforcement (MUST READ)\" section at the top of the\n  state.yaml schema block explaining WHY adherence matters (the\n  compaction hook parses specific names; deviations break recovery).\n- Updates the \"Recovery via state.yaml\" and \"Recovery Semantics —\n  Review→Completion Auto-Flow\" sections to use the new field names.\n- Adds a strict directive to ORCHESTRATOR.{md,opencode.md,copilot.md}\n  Post-Phase Protocol step 2: \"Write state.yaml STRICTLY per schema.\n  Use ONLY the field names listed. Do NOT invent any other fields. If\n  you think a new field is needed, the answer is no — propose a\n  contract change first.\"\n\nPairs with the compaction hook rewrite in the next commit, which now\nrelies on the canonical field names being stable.\n\n* fix(workflows/sdd): rewrite compaction hook — drop defensive prose, fix field parsing, skip terminal\n\nThe previous compaction hook was written before PR-A / audit and had\naccumulated four bugs that surfaced in session-ses_1ed8.md:\n\n1. Re-injects the \"Role Invariant\" defensive block (\"you orchestrate,\n   you do not implement... you do NOT: ...create branches/commits/PRs\n   ... If your next planned action is on the do-not list, you have\n   lost the role\"). PR-A removed this from ORCHESTRATOR.opencode.md;\n   the hook re-introduced it on every compaction, undoing the cleanup.\n2. Tells the orchestrator to \"Load Skill(sdd-orchestrator)\" — exactly\n   the Skill-tool jailbreak we diagnosed in ses_1f12. The orchestrator\n   IS the active primary agent in opencode.json; loading itself fetches\n   stale residues from .claude/skills/ (Anthropic syntax) or other\n   locations.\n3. References the old \"AskUserQuestion\" tool name (audit PR #66\n   replaced it with `question` for OpenCode) and the old \"create\n   branches\" prohibition (P3 #63 made workflow-init branch creation\n   allowed).\n4. Parses state.yaml with regexes for `current_phase` and `next_step`,\n   but the canonical schema (now aligned in the previous commit) uses\n   `phase` and `next`. Result: every recovery push said\n   \"phase=unknown / NEXT=check state.yaml\".\n\nPlus: embeds the full state.yaml content inline, which the orchestrator\ncan Read on demand if needed.\n\nThe new hook (~50 lines, half the size):\n\n- Reads only `phase` and `next` (canonical schema), no `unknown` paths\n  for normal workflows.\n- Pushes a single short block: workflow name, state file path, phase\n  and next values. The orchestrator''s playbook (in opencode.json) tells\n  it what to do with `next`; no need to repeat instructions.\n- Skips the recovery push entirely when the workflow has reached a\n  terminal phase (`phase: done` or `next: done`) — re-injecting\n  recovery directives after completion only invites re-doing finished\n  work.\n- Adds an explicit \"do NOT produce an orientation sentence\" directive\n  in the pushed context. This closes the \"I''ll continue with the next\n  step:\" pattern observed in session-ses_1ed8.md (line 3872) at the\n  layer where it makes sense (post-compaction is the only time the\n  model has reasonable license to \"re-orient\"), without patching the\n  orchestrator''s generic Forbidden table.\n\nPairs with the schema/enforce changes in the previous commit. Together\nthey make state.yaml + the recovery hook a coherent contract.\n\n* fix(workflows/sdd): address PR #67 review — drop defensive prose, rename to Hard Rules, move recovery semantics\n\nFour review comments addressed:\n\n- L100 catch-all row removed (user: \"el agente deberia ya saber que no\n  puedo agregar mas campos que los del schema propuesto\"). The per-field\n  forbidden table already enumerates the rejected fields with rationale;\n  the catch-all \"any other field\" row was meta-defensive prose adding no\n  signal.\n\n- L100 \"Schema Enforcement (MUST READ)\" callout dropped. Same spirit:\n  the agent reads the canonical schema + the forbidden table; the\n  callout was defensive framing without new content. The orchestrator''s\n  Post-Phase Protocol step 2 directive (\"Write state.yaml STRICTLY per\n  schema\") remains as the single enforcement point.\n\n- L102 \"Write Rules\" renamed to \"Hard Rules\" (user direct request) —\n  shorter and more authoritative section name.\n\n- L46 intro rewritten as a redirect (user: \"deberiamos redirigir al\n  agente segun de donde se lea este file\"). The intro now points to\n  recovery.md for recovery semantics. The \"Recovery via state.yaml\"\n  and \"Recovery Semantics — Review→Completion Auto-Flow\" sections\n  moved out of persistence-contract.md and into recovery.md, where\n  they architecturally belong (this file is about persistence; the\n  other is about recovery). recovery.md was also updated to use the\n  canonical field names (`phase`/`phase_status`/`next`) and its own\n  defensive Role Invariant block was dropped (the orchestrator already\n  has its playbook).\n\n- sdd-compaction.ts L66 directive (\"Do NOT produce an orientation\n  sentence...\") removed (user: \"no pasa nada si el agente me dice lo\n  que hara despues...esto tambien ayudara al usuario a ''pararlo''\").\n  Treating the post-compact narration as a useful safety net (user can\n  steer/stop) instead of forbidden noise.","tree":{"sha":"1db8bf0e5915b5dc833d937495d1c4f2ce238e7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/trees/1db8bf0e5915b5dc833d937495d1c4f2ce238e7d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/commits/a63883bad44136e9407d45c6f74f704e2149224d","verification":{"payload":"tree 1db8bf0e5915b5dc833d937495d1c4f2ce238e7d\nparent d047e5c6b989cc9e4e6625d41dc6d506a0351016\nauthor David Arce <davidarce2915@gmail.com> 1778434319 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778434319 +0200\n\nfix(workflows/sdd): compaction hook + persistence-contract enforcement (#67)\n\n* fix(workflows/sdd): align persistence-contract with canonical state.yaml schema + enforce\n\nThe orchestrator (Opus 4.7 in session-ses_1ed8.md) wrote a state.yaml\nthat diverged significantly from the documented contract:\n- Field names differed (`phase` vs `current_phase`, `next` vs\n  `last_envelope.next_recommended`, `phase_status` vs `status`).\n- Extra fields were invented (`project`, `branch`, `engram:` map,\n  `risks:`, `gates:`, `notes:`, `implement:`, `created`, `updated`).\n- One field was an outright contract violation: `artifacts:` is\n  documented as \"Explicitly NOT in state.yaml\" but was written anyway.\n\nThe contract was unenforceable because the schema was loose and the\norchestrator instructions only said \"per schema\" without \"STRICTLY\".\nResult: the OpenCode compaction hook (which parses by exact field\nnames) reported `Current phase: unknown / NEXT: check state.yaml`\nbecause its regexes did not match what the orchestrator actually wrote.\n\nThis change:\n\n- Adopts the orchestrator''s natural canonical names as the documented\n  schema (`phase`, `phase_status`, `next`) — they are simpler and the\n  contract now matches reality.\n- Allows the useful additions Opus invented as OPTIONAL fields:\n  `project`, `branch`, `engram:` map. These help cross-session recovery\n  without bloating state.\n- Explicitly forbids fields that duplicate information available\n  elsewhere: `artifacts:` (filesystem), `gates:` (envelope), `risks:`\n  (plan.md), `notes:`, `implement:` (derivable from `[X]` markers in\n  plan.md), `created`/`updated` (use `last_updated` ISO 8601).\n- Adds a \"Schema Enforcement (MUST READ)\" section at the top of the\n  state.yaml schema block explaining WHY adherence matters (the\n  compaction hook parses specific names; deviations break recovery).\n- Updates the \"Recovery via state.yaml\" and \"Recovery Semantics —\n  Review→Completion Auto-Flow\" sections to use the new field names.\n- Adds a strict directive to ORCHESTRATOR.{md,opencode.md,copilot.md}\n  Post-Phase Protocol step 2: \"Write state.yaml STRICTLY per schema.\n  Use ONLY the field names listed. Do NOT invent any other fields. If\n  you think a new field is needed, the answer is no — propose a\n  contract change first.\"\n\nPairs with the compaction hook rewrite in the next commit, which now\nrelies on the canonical field names being stable.\n\n* fix(workflows/sdd): rewrite compaction hook — drop defensive prose, fix field parsing, skip terminal\n\nThe previous compaction hook was written before PR-A / audit and had\naccumulated four bugs that surfaced in session-ses_1ed8.md:\n\n1. Re-injects the \"Role Invariant\" defensive block (\"you orchestrate,\n   you do not implement... you do NOT: ...create branches/commits/PRs\n   ... If your next planned action is on the do-not list, you have\n   lost the role\"). PR-A removed this from ORCHESTRATOR.opencode.md;\n   the hook re-introduced it on every compaction, undoing the cleanup.\n2. Tells the orchestrator to \"Load Skill(sdd-orchestrator)\" — exactly\n   the Skill-tool jailbreak we diagnosed in ses_1f12. The orchestrator\n   IS the active primary agent in opencode.json; loading itself fetches\n   stale residues from .claude/skills/ (Anthropic syntax) or other\n   locations.\n3. References the old \"AskUserQuestion\" tool name (audit PR #66\n   replaced it with `question` for OpenCode) and the old \"create\n   branches\" prohibition (P3 #63 made workflow-init branch creation\n   allowed).\n4. Parses state.yaml with regexes for `current_phase` and `next_step`,\n   but the canonical schema (now aligned in the previous commit) uses\n   `phase` and `next`. Result: every recovery push said\n   \"phase=unknown / NEXT=check state.yaml\".\n\nPlus: embeds the full state.yaml content inline, which the orchestrator\ncan Read on demand if needed.\n\nThe new hook (~50 lines, half the size):\n\n- Reads only `phase` and `next` (canonical schema), no `unknown` paths\n  for normal workflows.\n- Pushes a single short block: workflow name, state file path, phase\n  and next values. The orchestrator''s playbook (in opencode.json) tells\n  it what to do with `next`; no need to repeat instructions.\n- Skips the recovery push entirely when the workflow has reached a\n  terminal phase (`phase: done` or `next: done`) — re-injecting\n  recovery directives after completion only invites re-doing finished\n  work.\n- Adds an explicit \"do NOT produce an orientation sentence\" directive\n  in the pushed context. This closes the \"I''ll continue with the next\n  step:\" pattern observed in session-ses_1ed8.md (line 3872) at the\n  layer where it makes sense (post-compaction is the only time the\n  model has reasonable license to \"re-orient\"), without patching the\n  orchestrator''s generic Forbidden table.\n\nPairs with the schema/enforce changes in the previous commit. Together\nthey make state.yaml + the recovery hook a coherent contract.\n\n* fix(workflows/sdd): address PR #67 review — drop defensive prose, rename to Hard Rules, move recovery semantics\n\nFour review comments addressed:\n\n- L100 catch-all row removed (user: \"el agente deberia ya saber que no\n  puedo agregar mas campos que los del schema propuesto\"). The per-field\n  forbidden table already enumerates the rejected fields with rationale;\n  the catch-all \"any other field\" row was meta-defensive prose adding no\n  signal.\n\n- L100 \"Schema Enforcement (MUST READ)\" callout dropped. Same spirit:\n  the agent reads the canonical schema + the forbidden table; the\n  callout was defensive framing without new content. The orchestrator''s\n  Post-Phase Protocol step 2 directive (\"Write state.yaml STRICTLY per\n  schema\") remains as the single enforcement point.\n\n- L102 \"Write Rules\" renamed to \"Hard Rules\" (user direct request) —\n  shorter and more authoritative section name.\n\n- L46 intro rewritten as a redirect (user: \"deberiamos redirigir al\n  agente segun de donde se lea este file\"). The intro now points to\n  recovery.md for recovery semantics. The \"Recovery via state.yaml\"\n  and \"Recovery Semantics — Review→Completion Auto-Flow\" sections\n  moved out of persistence-contract.md and into recovery.md, where\n  they architecturally belong (this file is about persistence; the\n  other is about recovery). recovery.md was also updated to use the\n  canonical field names (`phase`/`phase_status`/`next`) and its own\n  defensive Role Invariant block was dropped (the orchestrator already\n  has its playbook).\n\n- sdd-compaction.ts L66 directive (\"Do NOT produce an orientation\n  sentence...\") removed (user: \"no pasa nada si el agente me dice lo\n  que hara despues...esto tambien ayudara al usuario a ''pararlo''\").\n  Treating the post-compact narration as a useful safety net (user can\n  steer/stop) instead of forbidden noise.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAMEPCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXCgQAARKxdtwRGd3+VLMyO4lALq6\n/+8cfBnTwgtF16r9Fb+p5BoqhWROOQkaOsbzmrm7Fj+ZqU+klWfCL2ymSAkxcgmG\neOpS5tfv5dWKHBLmPnpT2phOfj5B/kXt5DECOhYnnYGaXMi14T7QG48S589gGUKV\nMPLyPOUjyUlizRioxfYzNVvjIMg7ZbTRBXHckFS5V0yHKRhhZOEF2w/fwzm3+Nap\nBVOoOPNNfZGlqpgx4ywkakOX4vDmKgJW5ASyfYTrB2wMPRZWhTwyMKlpr82DgXd2\nx2WRD3htsWsCboe3oSL/kBf5SeNSQ6UExUG+UFIlgapJibIv0MDRR4X88IfirVFb\nPQxN3XfX3liTRmyduxQrwndQ1BmkT30ZxUMyUyLmA1hsynI+xRAeRkmv7mach8wB\nINpb79QP14udHmdZFCnI0Y2HXTe8MImA6uVZ7qtNdrfAdfOZ8HL+YLjuSxk3OwGg\nA0ZHgNbmnhQqG2OCFlTPXVaUzQraEgA6LRpzvDDNpduB8jtRiH/Gap0eJp/8Wh8M\narwxJUm24Iv6/znqZ1aquxQ61RrVzLk93bWAF1iX/Dkf1n0Rvvk3MG8BFNfAsk28\ngh89LVA0xggtoOBs/D2/UjpFoLDCeUPFpXPVmoPqSU2GG2DweagGbzjp9H/tb+fR\nrahN2FhfA7aeDVFqxr9C\n=9nth\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-10T17:32:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commit/a63883bad44136e9407d45c6f74f704e2149224d","node_id":"C_kwDORwxuadoAKGE2Mzg4M2JhZDQ0MTM2ZTk0MDdkNDVjNmY3NGY3MDRlMjE0OTIyNGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commit/d047e5c6b989cc9e4e6625d41dc6d506a0351016","sha":"d047e5c6b989cc9e4e6625d41dc6d506a0351016","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/d047e5c6b989cc9e4e6625d41dc6d506a0351016"}],"sha":"a63883bad44136e9407d45c6f74f704e2149224d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/a63883bad44136e9407d45c6f74f704e2149224d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13999850?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce","id":13999850,"login":"davidarce","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTk5ODUw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/d047e5c6b989cc9e4e6625d41dc6d506a0351016/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T17:19:51Z","email":"davidarce2915@gmail.com","name":"David Arce"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T17:19:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(workflows/sdd): orchestrator audit — Crit path, tool names, narration tightening, envelope contract (#66)\n\nFindings from observing a real OpenCode SDD session driven by Opus 4.7\n(session-ses_1ed8.md). Opus completed the workflow end-to-end, but the\nsession surfaced friction points that would cripple weaker models\n(gpt-5.5 already hit the same patterns). All seven improvements are\nin this single PR.\n\n## A. Crit feedback path bug fix\n\nCatalog instructions said `~/.crit/plans/{change}/.crit.json`. The\ndaemon actually writes `~/.crit/plans/{change}/.crit/review.json`.\nOpus discovered the correct path from the daemon''s own response and\nrecovered. A weaker model would have followed the wrong path and never\nread the feedback.\n\nFixed in: ORCHESTRATOR.md / ORCHESTRATOR.{claude,copilot,opencode}.md.\n\n## B. Pre-action narration: explicit examples added\n\nOld table covered \"Let me / I''ll / Now I''ll...\" but did not catch the\nphase-transition narration patterns observed in the session:\n\"Auto-launching plan\", \"Re-lanzo Crit para Round 2\", \"Cambio a una rama\nnueva...\". Added these as concrete ❌ rows in the OpenCode and Copilot\nvariants so the model has direct examples to match against.\n\n## C. bash echo as marker — explicitly forbidden\n\nObserved twice in the session: `bash: echo \"Question for user\"`\nfollowed by an actual question. The model treated the no-op echo as a\nrequired tool-call before \"speaking\". Added a dedicated forbidden table\nthat calls out the question tool (`question` for OpenCode,\n`vscode/askQuestions` for Copilot) as a valid action without any\npreceding marker.\n\n## D. Batch tasks must point to plan.md, NOT paraphrase\n\nThe orchestrator was re-stating ~1000 chars of task contract from\nplan.md inside each batch sub-agent prompt. Added a blockquote in the\nImplement section telling the orchestrator to fill the Sequential Batch\nTemplate with batch ID + path to plan.md only. Source-of-truth stays in\nplan.md; no drift, fewer tokens, less thinking time.\n\n## E. Tool names corrected per agent\n\nCatalog used `AskUserQuestion` everywhere. That is the Claude tool name.\n- OpenCode''s tool is `question` (per opencode.ai/docs/tools).\n- Copilot''s tool is `vscode/askQuestions` (per VS Code Copilot docs,\n  invoked as `#tool:vscode/askQuestions`).\n\nORCHESTRATOR.opencode.md now uses `question`. ORCHESTRATOR.copilot.md\npoints at `#tool:vscode/askQuestions`. ORCHESTRATOR.claude.md and\nORCHESTRATOR.md (generic) keep the original `AskUserQuestion` /\ngeneric phrasing.\n\n## F. Envelope contract reinforcement\n\nAdded a \"common drift patterns\" table to envelope-contract.md covering:\n- ASCII art frames around the envelope (observed in session-ses_1f19)\n- Restating the envelope as bullets after the table\n- \"Listo para siguiente fase:\" follow-up prose\n- Extra non-template fields (Effort, Confidence, etc.)\n\nThe \"envelope is the FINAL output\" rule is now phrased as parser-grade\n(\"anything after the closing risk bullet is discarded as drift\").\n\n## G. Outcome statements removed from Allowed classes\n\nOld \"Allowed — only these four classes\" included \"Outcome statements\nwhen a phase / wave / commit closes — one line\". This invited narration\nlike \"Plan aprobado vía Crit. Actualizo state y lanzo implement.\" after\nEVERY transition. The sub-agent envelope already conveys what closed.\n\nThe Allowed list now has THREE classes: Questions, Envelope summaries,\nErrors/blockers. Explicit note explains that outcome statements are\nabsorbed into class 1 (Questions) when the next user move is a decision.\n\nFiles touched:\n- workflows/sdd/ORCHESTRATOR.md\n- workflows/sdd/ORCHESTRATOR.claude.md\n- workflows/sdd/ORCHESTRATOR.copilot.md\n- workflows/sdd/ORCHESTRATOR.opencode.md\n- workflows/sdd/_shared/envelope-contract.md","tree":{"sha":"13527807bd0c4329f41364621262cebff704e31d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/trees/13527807bd0c4329f41364621262cebff704e31d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/commits/d047e5c6b989cc9e4e6625d41dc6d506a0351016","verification":{"payload":"tree 13527807bd0c4329f41364621262cebff704e31d\nparent b44265166224d3926183d8ebe3b7c6fb9a857fa3\nauthor David Arce <davidarce2915@gmail.com> 1778433591 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778433591 +0200\n\nfix(workflows/sdd): orchestrator audit — Crit path, tool names, narration tightening, envelope contract (#66)\n\nFindings from observing a real OpenCode SDD session driven by Opus 4.7\n(session-ses_1ed8.md). Opus completed the workflow end-to-end, but the\nsession surfaced friction points that would cripple weaker models\n(gpt-5.5 already hit the same patterns). All seven improvements are\nin this single PR.\n\n## A. Crit feedback path bug fix\n\nCatalog instructions said `~/.crit/plans/{change}/.crit.json`. The\ndaemon actually writes `~/.crit/plans/{change}/.crit/review.json`.\nOpus discovered the correct path from the daemon''s own response and\nrecovered. A weaker model would have followed the wrong path and never\nread the feedback.\n\nFixed in: ORCHESTRATOR.md / ORCHESTRATOR.{claude,copilot,opencode}.md.\n\n## B. Pre-action narration: explicit examples added\n\nOld table covered \"Let me / I''ll / Now I''ll...\" but did not catch the\nphase-transition narration patterns observed in the session:\n\"Auto-launching plan\", \"Re-lanzo Crit para Round 2\", \"Cambio a una rama\nnueva...\". Added these as concrete ❌ rows in the OpenCode and Copilot\nvariants so the model has direct examples to match against.\n\n## C. bash echo as marker — explicitly forbidden\n\nObserved twice in the session: `bash: echo \"Question for user\"`\nfollowed by an actual question. The model treated the no-op echo as a\nrequired tool-call before \"speaking\". Added a dedicated forbidden table\nthat calls out the question tool (`question` for OpenCode,\n`vscode/askQuestions` for Copilot) as a valid action without any\npreceding marker.\n\n## D. Batch tasks must point to plan.md, NOT paraphrase\n\nThe orchestrator was re-stating ~1000 chars of task contract from\nplan.md inside each batch sub-agent prompt. Added a blockquote in the\nImplement section telling the orchestrator to fill the Sequential Batch\nTemplate with batch ID + path to plan.md only. Source-of-truth stays in\nplan.md; no drift, fewer tokens, less thinking time.\n\n## E. Tool names corrected per agent\n\nCatalog used `AskUserQuestion` everywhere. That is the Claude tool name.\n- OpenCode''s tool is `question` (per opencode.ai/docs/tools).\n- Copilot''s tool is `vscode/askQuestions` (per VS Code Copilot docs,\n  invoked as `#tool:vscode/askQuestions`).\n\nORCHESTRATOR.opencode.md now uses `question`. ORCHESTRATOR.copilot.md\npoints at `#tool:vscode/askQuestions`. ORCHESTRATOR.claude.md and\nORCHESTRATOR.md (generic) keep the original `AskUserQuestion` /\ngeneric phrasing.\n\n## F. Envelope contract reinforcement\n\nAdded a \"common drift patterns\" table to envelope-contract.md covering:\n- ASCII art frames around the envelope (observed in session-ses_1f19)\n- Restating the envelope as bullets after the table\n- \"Listo para siguiente fase:\" follow-up prose\n- Extra non-template fields (Effort, Confidence, etc.)\n\nThe \"envelope is the FINAL output\" rule is now phrased as parser-grade\n(\"anything after the closing risk bullet is discarded as drift\").\n\n## G. Outcome statements removed from Allowed classes\n\nOld \"Allowed — only these four classes\" included \"Outcome statements\nwhen a phase / wave / commit closes — one line\". This invited narration\nlike \"Plan aprobado vía Crit. Actualizo state y lanzo implement.\" after\nEVERY transition. The sub-agent envelope already conveys what closed.\n\nThe Allowed list now has THREE classes: Questions, Envelope summaries,\nErrors/blockers. Explicit note explains that outcome statements are\nabsorbed into class 1 (Questions) when the next user move is a decision.\n\nFiles touched:\n- workflows/sdd/ORCHESTRATOR.md\n- workflows/sdd/ORCHESTRATOR.claude.md\n- workflows/sdd/ORCHESTRATOR.copilot.md\n- workflows/sdd/ORCHESTRATOR.opencode.md\n- workflows/sdd/_shared/envelope-contract.md","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAL43CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQewQAD4u3Uuok2azvKHu1ZernXV5\nrhp3n73UkGKl6iQX4koY7cDLv2zlk0IABjjOPAO7Lppp/R0L1gVUc5GPGFpbeaNk\np1uUZMnE3/hbePiFm6Elmb3gJJkj8Pf/OyzdvEZH3PYMwDYyhZ8N+A2YCdbz86TR\ni18e9omrNurFEz1c/sLJB5nHL7nN9M0sy8uKcNE3qOFQkeuibeRbyx+jlzjKpZs3\n+EwzNYIfJqV6FyZIHtHIyo1W9A6ZQQGRhi6V8czstV37Mv4Q1hbLLBTBVb1JG1Kk\nm3MrDFQ0iY6ZNfCOp2h7w87Ym11bcDrK5zog4VobzMeRDvsx67LbA+ibKig82yZO\nR6DV5AdY7KL4aXJayYO2wbua5pb+L0Hb1ej4hK9KNwD1PRAywU6okkTYL1gYqh3N\nuku3QMZVqvHSewRHt69+9Fx66tppAu8L0pZdK