bscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commit/b44265166224d3926183d8ebe3b7c6fb9a857fa3","node_id":"C_kwDORwxuadoAKGI0NDI2NTE2NjIyNGQzOTI2MTgzZDhlYmUzYjdjNmZiOWE4NTdmYTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commit/d4037fa099f4e9b6091df86763250f1be74f5cde","sha":"d4037fa099f4e9b6091df86763250f1be74f5cde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/d4037fa099f4e9b6091df86763250f1be74f5cde"}],"sha":"b44265166224d3926183d8ebe3b7c6fb9a857fa3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/b44265166224d3926183d8ebe3b7c6fb9a857fa3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13999850?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce","id":13999850,"login":"davidarce","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTk5ODUw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/d4037fa099f4e9b6091df86763250f1be74f5cde/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T15:37:23Z","email":"davidarce2915@gmail.com","name":"David Arce"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T15:37:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(workflows/sdd): smarter engram guard — recover from \"ambiguous project\" (#64)\n\nThe previous engram availability guard collapsed two distinct failure\nmodes into the same \"engram unavailable\" outcome:\n\n1. Engram MCP server not installed / not running (genuine unavailability).\n2. Engram IS installed but the cwd contains multiple git sub-repos and\n   engram cannot pick a default project (recoverable with one extra call).\n\nCase (2) is the common \"monorepo-style workspace\" scenario. A recent\nOpenCode SDD test in `libraries/` hit it: `mem_context()` failed with\n\"ambiguous project: multiple git repos found in cwd\", the orchestrator\ndeclared engram unavailable, never wrote the active-workflow marker,\nand lost the recovery path entirely.\n\nThis change updates the guard pattern in:\n- `ORCHESTRATOR.opencode.md`\n- `ORCHESTRATOR.copilot.md`\n- `_shared/persistence-contract.md`\n\nNew behaviour:\n- `mem_context()` succeeds → cache `engram_available=true` and the\n  project engram resolved (`engram_project`).\n- Fails with \"tool not found\" / \"MCP server not running\" → genuinely\n  unavailable, skip silently as before.\n- Fails with \"ambiguous project\" / \"multiple git repos\" → recover by\n  calling `mem_current_project()` (engram''s built-in disambiguation\n  helper). If it returns a project name, cache it and pass it on every\n  later engram call; tell the user once that engram resolved to that\n  project and suggest `.engram/config.json` for an explicit pin.\n- Any other error → fail-safe to unavailable.\n\nAt most ONE disambiguation retry. No retry loops.\n\nAlso includes `.engram/config.json` for the catalog repo itself\n(`{\"project_name\": \"devrune-starter-catalog\"}`) so anyone cloning the\ncatalog as a standalone workspace gets engram pre-configured.","tree":{"sha":"8f9051d231e83b1ce8844cbed510b378f342d6ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/trees/8f9051d231e83b1ce8844cbed510b378f342d6ed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/commits/d4037fa099f4e9b6091df86763250f1be74f5cde","verification":{"payload":"tree 8f9051d231e83b1ce8844cbed510b378f342d6ed\nparent 10245c54b35cbfb9a1836c24fc9e9461006fda62\nauthor David Arce <davidarce2915@gmail.com> 1778427443 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778427443 +0200\n\nfix(workflows/sdd): smarter engram guard — recover from \"ambiguous project\" (#64)\n\nThe previous engram availability guard collapsed two distinct failure\nmodes into the same \"engram unavailable\" outcome:\n\n1. Engram MCP server not installed / not running (genuine unavailability).\n2. Engram IS installed but the cwd contains multiple git sub-repos and\n   engram cannot pick a default project (recoverable with one extra call).\n\nCase (2) is the common \"monorepo-style workspace\" scenario. A recent\nOpenCode SDD test in `libraries/` hit it: `mem_context()` failed with\n\"ambiguous project: multiple git repos found in cwd\", the orchestrator\ndeclared engram unavailable, never wrote the active-workflow marker,\nand lost the recovery path entirely.\n\nThis change updates the guard pattern in:\n- `ORCHESTRATOR.opencode.md`\n- `ORCHESTRATOR.copilot.md`\n- `_shared/persistence-contract.md`\n\nNew behaviour:\n- `mem_context()` succeeds → cache `engram_available=true` and the\n  project engram resolved (`engram_project`).\n- Fails with \"tool not found\" / \"MCP server not running\" → genuinely\n  unavailable, skip silently as before.\n- Fails with \"ambiguous project\" / \"multiple git repos\" → recover by\n  calling `mem_current_project()` (engram''s built-in disambiguation\n  helper). If it returns a project name, cache it and pass it on every\n  later engram call; tell the user once that engram resolved to that\n  project and suggest `.engram/config.json` for an explicit pin.\n- Any other error → fail-safe to unavailable.\n\nAt most ONE disambiguation retry. No retry loops.\n\nAlso includes `.engram/config.json` for the catalog repo itself\n(`{\"project_name\": \"devrune-starter-catalog\"}`) so anyone cloning the\ncatalog as a standalone workspace gets engram pre-configured.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAKYzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4v4QAH4Uq2eIi2MpjQfNkmXsHkXm\n1Bv78wL9m5YLCJOHw09e1/6G2GGXrvUAr9TTM1FJBbUyEhDNSgNeqEzb83LvnWVV\n/j5fPTKoA5MtQ4nbUZqnlj7pHW5E6Xcy1QJjuSbxtvsH4FpaLYVbnYKmX8gjD1Wd\nW2l5BBbnMzuyhlLi3RXYg05QvAkeyaUeaOAQ6pzv509MzHNw451NpXV9JmE0Symx\naHPFPME49U3K46p44ZOSRLpGh6Ui6PEEAyHB+Tz2yQbGGPiEKSE8ZWdRjjcWyGi6\nfA0jW3DgLWrvACfOC0nq6QxZYcOdbaSMEqBEwtp+YGyAJigz91lOGLEBdnxqZpfU\ns4HVWQf1HncI+GLYdbS8B4AcimjwTgFv5/oVAdwMUSLXDWwxH5u+BgNATBp97bTh\nMk2H1/ve9fB9XlLmROqimKF0WF99pAg7w6HSluO5s+n5qKH4RwyNwQFRr4watvAu\na8aezHzI0dJAzKnTZfy3SZgQc8Q241HZdV5aRgYmOmtZhAwz0HRqwUK++gs+yUrk\nXwA55G/nFn0JHzUxHiwGQXkNyxkDwSmP20Kc5PHce/KC/StTqqAMiV6CADT6kcCn\nom7kDJdf00PcpYDAkRsSW5/u5iF/nxC0lSGk1l5LHeM8KsVYzfH1LE29C+pm3bJy\nD54CLw3b4tNmrexTOwvr\n=AwtC\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-10T15:37:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commit/d4037fa099f4e9b6091df86763250f1be74f5cde","node_id":"C_kwDORwxuadoAKGQ0MDM3ZmEwOTlmNGU5YjYwOTFkZjg2NzYzMjUwZjFiZTc0ZjVjZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commit/10245c54b35cbfb9a1836c24fc9e9461006fda62","sha":"10245c54b35cbfb9a1836c24fc9e9461006fda62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/10245c54b35cbfb9a1836c24fc9e9461006fda62"}],"sha":"d4037fa099f4e9b6091df86763250f1be74f5cde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/d4037fa099f4e9b6091df86763250f1be74f5cde"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13999850?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce","id":13999850,"login":"davidarce","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTk5ODUw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/10245c54b35cbfb9a1836c24fc9e9461006fda62/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T15:36:54Z","email":"davidarce2915@gmail.com","name":"David Arce"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T15:36:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(workflows/sdd): git pre-flight guard + allow workflow-init branch creation (#63)\n\nTwo related fixes for the orchestrator''s Branch setup step:\n\n1. Pre-flight git guard.\n\n   Before running `git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD`, the orchestrator\n   now checks `git rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree` and skips Step 3\n   entirely when the cwd is not inside a git repository. Common case:\n   a monorepo-style workspace that aggregates multiple sub-repos at the\n   root, where the root itself has no .git/.\n\n   Without this guard, the orchestrator ran three failing git commands\n   silently (each returning \"fatal: not a git repository\") and continued\n   without telling the user. Now it tells the user once and skips the\n   step; sub-agents still run their own git commands inside the relevant\n   sub-repo.\n\n   Applied to ORCHESTRATOR.md / ORCHESTRATOR.opencode.md /\n   ORCHESTRATOR.copilot.md.\n\n2. Remove \"create branches\" from the \"you do not\" defensive list.\n\n   REGISTRY.md / REGISTRY.claude.md / ORCHESTRATOR.md previously said\n   \"you do not: ... create branches/commits/PRs\". This contradicted the\n   Branch setup step, which legitimately runs `git checkout -b ...` as\n   part of workflow initialization. The contradiction was caught by\n   gpt-5.5 in a recent OpenCode test (\"the orchestrator restrictions say\n   not to create branches, which is confusing\").\n\n   Branch creation here is workflow init, not a commit-mutating action.\n   The \"no git commit / push\" rule still holds — those belong to the\n   git-commit and git-pull-request skills at the end of the workflow.\n   An explicit blockquote note now spells out that distinction next to\n   the Branch setup step in all three orchestrator variants.","tree":{"sha":"772cb3ad60f0359ec7524598b209707e00d78abb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/trees/772cb3ad60f0359ec7524598b209707e00d78abb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/commits/10245c54b35cbfb9a1836c24fc9e9461006fda62","verification":{"payload":"tree 772cb3ad60f0359ec7524598b209707e00d78abb\nparent eadc2464a5a303d28d2c7c2c7df778de3f7016bc\nauthor David Arce <davidarce2915@gmail.com> 1778427414 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778427414 +0200\n\nfix(workflows/sdd): git pre-flight guard + allow workflow-init branch creation (#63)\n\nTwo related fixes for the orchestrator''s Branch setup step:\n\n1. Pre-flight git guard.\n\n   Before running `git rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD`, the orchestrator\n   now checks `git rev-parse --is-inside-work-tree` and skips Step 3\n   entirely when the cwd is not inside a git repository. Common case:\n   a monorepo-style workspace that aggregates multiple sub-repos at the\n   root, where the root itself has no .git/.\n\n   Without this guard, the orchestrator ran three failing git commands\n   silently (each returning \"fatal: not a git repository\") and continued\n   without telling the user. Now it tells the user once and skips the\n   step; sub-agents still run their own git commands inside the relevant\n   sub-repo.\n\n   Applied to ORCHESTRATOR.md / ORCHESTRATOR.opencode.md /\n   ORCHESTRATOR.copilot.md.\n\n2. Remove \"create branches\" from the \"you do not\" defensive list.\n\n   REGISTRY.md / REGISTRY.claude.md / ORCHESTRATOR.md previously said\n   \"you do not: ... create branches/commits/PRs\". This contradicted the\n   Branch setup step, which legitimately runs `git checkout -b ...` as\n   part of workflow initialization. The contradiction was caught by\n   gpt-5.5 in a recent OpenCode test (\"the orchestrator restrictions say\n   not to create branches, which is confusing\").\n\n   Branch creation here is workflow init, not a commit-mutating action.\n   The \"no git commit / push\" rule still holds — those belong to the\n   git-commit and git-pull-request skills at the end of the workflow.\n   An explicit blockquote note now spells out that distinction next to\n   the Branch setup step in all three orchestrator variants.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAKYWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEqQQADyooxz4m2iuqWUhJ90F9IMn\nIQprBHG8xGZ+5DlkEHYsbNc4GWCOsEj2yvYiqM8ZAos5I0e44/SAy0ZUbTKpaZm8\nScarRwn0b4cDUrQ0WgUBJGA62PmcucX9PAn73Lqt+TIt9J0ZSxTt4byLtEbpVGHS\nXwziN3oni8n3lRiSofDZ6HQnunEK+a1kYFhDtjb12WFOScr7AItzZq49BAo52eRA\nIb07594qTgihq2vmRutEraJAPAEd9p5jv9MJz3n9GxYWP6b/jKY9QN/HUckCUhx4\nMVvTo2etx2YmbeVyga/4TVoTjXu4TBRSCo+rej9J1EQJAe6u2BN4TgmMqkHwKVXz\nPIv8p/vuOMZZ+3yZt2Ics1OZOlNiu6dZ+hVY3o2TVaQKryEJG80RwvIMHrz5A93D\nqkazn3xa+5qsIhyBHPIUAtVQjuo37SbzcvhXO9qsPc3i7183eQ+Ji9LOrhdPFGJ7\nmE6ijyiMdT2J+70E9Z4H7SNyjRTlDwYttVGWoruaoN39cP6m6B++z/KXZuT5aGpr\nAs8hTfi7QM8cE7rHmum1MD09fjKHqE1wXBQ+BRNwZjNgtg2pmJxCHrQPN8H77n96\nhFIpw6grB/5t9D+v0/8hV0mxM3PbDfLklIpyt9H+AwTohRl8RCdIzYWYOQiPh1A5\n+AShLpunjEJun2U95Xmw\n=brfA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-10T15:36:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commit/10245c54b35cbfb9a1836c24fc9e9461006fda62","node_id":"C_kwDORwxuadoAKDEwMjQ1YzU0YjM1Y2JmYjlhMTgzNmMyNGZjOWU5NDYxMDA2ZmRhNjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commit/eadc2464a5a303d28d2c7c2c7df778de3f7016bc","sha":"eadc2464a5a303d28d2c7c2c7df778de3f7016bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/eadc2464a5a303d28d2c7c2c7df778de3f7016bc"}],"sha":"10245c54b35cbfb9a1836c24fc9e9461006fda62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/10245c54b35cbfb9a1836c24fc9e9461006fda62"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13999850?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce","id":13999850,"login":"davidarce","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTk5ODUw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/eadc2464a5a303d28d2c7c2c7df778de3f7016bc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T15:35:48Z","email":"davidarce2915@gmail.com","name":"David Arce"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T15:35:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(workflows/sdd): use {SHARED_DIR} placeholder instead of {WORKFLOW_DIR}/_shared/ (#62)\n\nTemplates now reference workflow-shared assets via the new {SHARED_DIR}\nplaceholder. The renderer resolves it to the agent-appropriate path:\n- Claude/Factory/Codex: still inside the orchestrator skill dir\n  (.{agent}/skills/sdd-orchestrator/_shared/) — the orchestrator IS a\n  real skill on disk, so its assets legitimately live inside it.\n- OpenCode/Copilot: workflow-namespaced top-level\n  (.opencode/sdd/_shared/, .github/sdd/_shared/) — the orchestrator is\n  a primary agent (in opencode.json / .agent.md), so the legacy\n  sdd-orchestrator/ directory was a fantasma container with no SKILL.md.\n\nThe placeholder keeps templates agnostic to where _shared/ ends up;\neach renderer resolves it idiomatically. {WORKFLOW_DIR} stays available\nfor any future template that needs to reference the orchestrator''s own\ndirectory (Claude/Factory/Codex skill dir).\n\nFiles touched:\n- ORCHESTRATOR.md / ORCHESTRATOR.{claude,copilot,opencode}.md\n- REGISTRY.md / REGISTRY.claude.md\n- _shared/launch-templates.opencode.md\n- _shared/recovery.md\n\nPairs with DevRune renderer change that introduces {SHARED_DIR} and\nmoves _shared/ install path for OpenCode/Copilot.","tree":{"sha":"943140ac55381320db1c5a206dbe60ce74163712","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/trees/943140ac55381320db1c5a206dbe60ce74163712"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/commits/eadc2464a5a303d28d2c7c2c7df778de3f7016bc","verification":{"payload":"tree 943140ac55381320db1c5a206dbe60ce74163712\nparent e91bc3e37a473e50880061470974d18559202cbf\nauthor David Arce <davidarce2915@gmail.com> 1778427348 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778427348 +0200\n\nrefactor(workflows/sdd): use {SHARED_DIR} placeholder instead of {WORKFLOW_DIR}/_shared/ (#62)\n\nTemplates now reference workflow-shared assets via the new {SHARED_DIR}\nplaceholder. The renderer resolves it to the agent-appropriate path:\n- Claude/Factory/Codex: still inside the orchestrator skill dir\n  (.{agent}/skills/sdd-orchestrator/_shared/) — the orchestrator IS a\n  real skill on disk, so its assets legitimately live inside it.\n- OpenCode/Copilot: workflow-namespaced top-level\n  (.opencode/sdd/_shared/, .github/sdd/_shared/) — the orchestrator is\n  a primary agent (in opencode.json / .agent.md), so the legacy\n  sdd-orchestrator/ directory was a fantasma container with no SKILL.md.\n\nThe placeholder keeps templates agnostic to where _shared/ ends up;\neach renderer resolves it idiomatically. {WORKFLOW_DIR} stays available\nfor any future template that needs to reference the orchestrator''s own\ndirectory (Claude/Factory/Codex skill dir).\n\nFiles touched:\n- ORCHESTRATOR.md / ORCHESTRATOR.{claude,copilot,opencode}.md\n- REGISTRY.md / REGISTRY.claude.md\n- _shared/launch-templates.opencode.md\n- _shared/recovery.md\n\nPairs with DevRune renderer change that introduces {SHARED_DIR} and\nmoves _shared/ install path for OpenCode/Copilot.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAKXUCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADuoQAIXxZGyUrM9jJzGK6vNoJztj\nxEiQO0gLtyiYFADUIkixEKZAHCY8TK8CkYiVO+QqebgTI+YGQcQvEAnnGa6PHcKS\nwGR1aruJ/3tnZteeKbf8ABwlTleuZpYEaLukqL3l8buoTzpOFTTR7ba13UUnp+U/\nM2GVyqR6VfQTs0zyxxDlnq/HuDnBcl19SO1CP/NxIBbRHdKv4FC131HetWVxSpwb\nw3VcTIqa1IIdVnFT+baSDSK4ACfuFBU0oFcDfv3JIpKvZZPyMqdRhjjQvjukX+U0\nWZC/lEGq51k9TXOzWCkH77UzVa9aAX9xSV0MUyWiq2PNGL9ypjJcpHSCskWGA4zi\nCeBtzfJ9wXeWvum3a74Y02kiatOWsGvNEspGMt9YimlapXTz9sJCUImT3zPdzsYZ\ngdQjjWqKl4lyCmiOpbEaDP5LfMzHWbS+Mu4oNp8ymzppkMzZ2JYo9wKQ+0EmyFmU\nWgGgAlnkJs1b0t0PIRcEoqjNW4Pi5UIc5WX4GA2t3nSqE8FrHJQd9XxlvRaAkivA\nq5q/JhIfVU1r3L+afcia+HsAMofxRaG822w4zsJ++XF37XB5v4TxaZP5Ep3K7DeH\ncsSDW9AlzXBpDecX/phZhdPYJsVr+7CTBn/vPSRvdV14CYDv+Efj4uCSOrvyP7X3\nrHcTktDLJKxXnpi+68a/\n=iWU6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-10T15:35:49Z"