g1NTkyMDJjYmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commit/aa87c06aaf2637b8f32d2848fdafeb53fb1468fc","sha":"aa87c06aaf2637b8f32d2848fdafeb53fb1468fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/aa87c06aaf2637b8f32d2848fdafeb53fb1468fc"}],"sha":"e91bc3e37a473e50880061470974d18559202cbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/e91bc3e37a473e50880061470974d18559202cbf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13999850?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce","id":13999850,"login":"davidarce","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTk5ODUw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/aa87c06aaf2637b8f32d2848fdafeb53fb1468fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-10T14:45:54Z","email":"davidarce2915@gmail.com","name":"David Arce"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-10T14:45:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(workflows/sdd): drop REGISTRY for OpenCode/Copilot, slim ORCHESTRATOR, reorder PRD gate (#60)\n\nOpenCode and Copilot have a primary `sdd-orchestrator` agent the user\nexplicitly selects (not an ambient catalog the main session has to read).\nThat selection IS the consent to use SDD; the orchestrator should not\nre-evaluate whether to start, defend its role, or duplicate ambient rules\nalready implicit in being the primary agent.\n\nThe REGISTRY pattern only makes sense for Claude/Factory, where there is\nno primary agent and CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md must carry the playbook for\nthe main session to know when to engage SDD. For OpenCode/Copilot, both\nthe catalog injection (AGENTS.md) and the orchestrator-prompt prepend\nwere leaking workflow-specific rules into non-workflow sessions and\nduplicating / contradicting the orchestrator''s own playbook.\n\nThree changes here, one in the renderer (separate PR):\n\n- ORCHESTRATOR.opencode.md / ORCHESTRATOR.copilot.md: rewritten as the\n  single source of the orchestrator playbook. Sections kept: language\n  matching, output discipline, launching sub-agents, Crit, batch\n  orchestration, post-review fix cycle, compaction recovery, memory\n  protocols, engram guard, gotchas. Sections dropped: \"Your Role\"\n  defensive prose, \"Evaluation Gate\" (user already chose), \"How to Start\"\n  decisional framing, \"Re-load skill\" defensive instructions.\n\n- Workflow Initialization reorder: workdir + active-workflow marker → PRD\n  gate → branch setup → auto-launch explore. Branch type is now informed\n  by PRD content (when present) instead of guessing from the raw user\n  prompt before scope is clarified.\n\n- REGISTRY.opencode.md / REGISTRY.copilot.md deleted. With the renderer\n  change (separate PR in DevRune) the variant resolver no longer reads\n  these files, so they are simply dead weight.\n\nREGISTRY.md (generic, used by Claude/Factory/Codex) is unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"08facf4d36c4b6ba202b2cbd906d3da369910099","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/trees/08facf4d36c4b6ba202b2cbd906d3da369910099"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/commits/aa87c06aaf2637b8f32d2848fdafeb53fb1468fc","verification":{"payload":"tree 08facf4d36c4b6ba202b2cbd906d3da369910099\nparent b8af6af9f9e6389b0a5b95a2b4953d34361a7842\nauthor David Arce <davidarce2915@gmail.com> 1778424354 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778424354 +0200\n\nfix(workflows/sdd): drop REGISTRY for OpenCode/Copilot, slim ORCHESTRATOR, reorder PRD gate (#60)\n\nOpenCode and Copilot have a primary `sdd-orchestrator` agent the user\nexplicitly selects (not an ambient catalog the main session has to read).\nThat selection IS the consent to use SDD; the orchestrator should not\nre-evaluate whether to start, defend its role, or duplicate ambient rules\nalready implicit in being the primary agent.\n\nThe REGISTRY pattern only makes sense for Claude/Factory, where there is\nno primary agent and CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md must carry the playbook for\nthe main session to know when to engage SDD. For OpenCode/Copilot, both\nthe catalog injection (AGENTS.md) and the orchestrator-prompt prepend\nwere leaking workflow-specific rules into non-workflow sessions and\nduplicating / contradicting the orchestrator''s own playbook.\n\nThree changes here, one in the renderer (separate PR):\n\n- ORCHESTRATOR.opencode.md / ORCHESTRATOR.copilot.md: rewritten as the\n  single source of the orchestrator playbook. Sections kept: language\n  matching, output discipline, launching sub-agents, Crit, batch\n  orchestration, post-review fix cycle, compaction recovery, memory\n  protocols, engram guard, gotchas. Sections dropped: \"Your Role\"\n  defensive prose, \"Evaluation Gate\" (user already chose), \"How to Start\"\n  decisional framing, \"Re-load skill\" defensive instructions.\n\n- Workflow Initialization reorder: workdir + active-workflow marker → PRD\n  gate → branch setup → auto-launch explore. Branch type is now informed\n  by PRD content (when present) instead of guessing from the raw user\n  prompt before scope is clarified.\n\n- REGISTRY.opencode.md / REGISTRY.copilot.md deleted. With the renderer\n  change (separate PR in DevRune) the variant resolver no longer reads\n  these files, so they are simply dead weight.\n\nREGISTRY.md (generic, used by Claude/Factory/Codex) is unchanged.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqAJoiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAk64QAH7uUQ4y3B0PwqHK5/+Dqj8h\n0xVTKo9tAHXOLDUvZCdv67arIfEXZ85OdVI8ji2YoKbY8rm2KFjJW30DeLuHrZhY\nxWylMn+FDcowZiO8YFxRAGhgH+FQPpyqXudOOUAQQZbjjwoDP3NtS6/UgFShcTCO\nTG6bA0m5pNclsq2bxJfQV564TKsQKOJ/nQn8j5jdFSMvgIRTMJp31EGdOR4FIQAW\nivt2oVhX8GDqGfugd/rV25liah+NxMZi9m+rbci5kJrK2OSLgdW5J4HWAaFIkuTW\nsLLm7hhTai7IMiGZquJSruGA3dNei0RUyaH5FuNfGKdx05navQkfRarpktnHNsna\n/F+TsA/m/I2RwzuM1Xf8X8rQgqiXLvdiR5qkDhBTkKRjgTzV/Jf6QhCpQX6wJvmn\nu44yBvNm2XxkkFM9ZMain3K6215MesULEV0gIO1qxrqtYXgEJX8Db2kGPVFR9tnZ\nJ4WElLqaaOd74U5SpbGLxsCu9rndsfrs0xpWSmSGxVWCU1dIdXrSEEehwq9c5siB\nEXotwS3kA32xee51RPkjzS4V/NUaCqBpl21usynkI1o1njGl2vjpgtuCn/5o+WPE\nfYKxZd84QJ60qw/BrMnaUGKBNkRoUSHasDLX5jrdZK+1WHvixylcESVBX6nSuyiI\no7O/8oqb8VcKn0e9+U1P\n=TzBY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-10T14:45:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","ur