evrune-starter-catalog/commits/d9d4a321438ef388e36a3e9a8927b858e4059b34"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13999850?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce","id":13999850,"login":"davidarce","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTk5ODUw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/d806733f3065bae55a553861aef934199a8227ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-09T21:54:38Z","email":"davidarce2915@gmail.com","name":"David Arce"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-09T21:54:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(workflows/sdd): align OpenCode orchestrator on Task() + WORKFLOW_SUBAGENT_ADVISOR (#56)\n\n* fix(workflows/sdd): align OpenCode orchestrator on Task() syntax + WORKFLOW_SUBAGENT_ADVISOR placeholder\n\nThe OpenCode orchestrator received contradictory invocation instructions\nbecause REGISTRY.opencode.md described `@<sub-agent>` natural-language\nmentions while ORCHESTRATOR.opencode.md (correctly) used `Task()`. The\ntwo blocks are concatenated into the synthesised orchestrator prompt,\nso the model saw both syntaxes and stalled deciding between them.\n\nIndependently, `_shared/advisor-templates.md` hardcoded\n`subagent_type: ''general-purpose''` for both the parallel and the\nsequential templates. The catalog already declares an `sdd-advisor`\nrole in `workflow.yaml`, and `{WORKFLOW_SUBAGENT_ADVISOR}` is the\nplaceholder DevRune resolves at install time — so the templates were\npointing at a non-existent agent for OpenCode (which exposes only the\nagents declared in `opencode.json`).\n\nChanges:\n- REGISTRY.opencode.md — replace `@<sub-agent>` / `@sdd-{phase}` with\n  `Task(subagent_type: ''{WORKFLOW_SUBAGENT_<PHASE>}'', ...)`. Aligns\n  with ORCHESTRATOR.opencode.md and removes the contradiction.\n- _shared/advisor-templates.md — swap `''general-purpose''` for\n  `''{WORKFLOW_SUBAGENT_ADVISOR}''` on both templates. Generic file is\n  still consumed by Claude/Factory; placeholder resolves to the\n  agent name declared in `workflow.yaml` per renderer.\n- _shared/advisor-templates.opencode.md (NEW) — OpenCode-only variant\n  with just the Sequential template + Plan Re-entry template, no\n  `model:` or `run_in_background:` fields (OpenCode resolves model\n  from the agent definition in opencode.json). Renderer renames it\n  to `advisor-templates.md` and suppresses the generic for OpenCode\n  installs, matching the existing pattern for `launch-templates`.\n\n* fix(workflows/sdd): drop redundant prose for OpenCode orchestrator\n\nThree follow-ups from PR #56 review — the agent already knows it is the\nsdd-orchestrator, already knows OpenCode''s run_in_background limitation,\nand already knows model is sourced from opencode.json. Saying so wastes\nprompt budget.\n\n- REGISTRY.opencode.md \"How to Start\": drop the \"you ARE the orchestrator\"\n  sentence; renumber from 1.\n- REGISTRY.opencode.md \"Compaction Recovery\": drop the same self-identity\n  step; move recovery.md path to the preamble; renumber from 1.\n- advisor-templates.opencode.md: drop the OpenCode-constraint callout and\n  the \"do not pass model:\" callout. The remaining Task() snippet shows\n  the correct shape on its own.\n\n* fix(workflows/sdd): drop OpenCode self-reference in advisor-templates header\n\nPR #56 follow-up: the file is renamed to advisor-templates.md at install\ntime, so ''(OpenCode)'' in the H1 and the ''OpenCode-only file'' HTML comment\nboth lose meaning in the materialised workspace. Removed both, plus the\nSYNC WITH note (catalog-maintainer concern, belongs in commit history /\ndocs not in the runtime artifact).","tree":{"sha":"85ea970ad589dc4e0de9d2e7b104243a41e82d5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/trees/85ea970ad589dc4e0de9d2e7b104243a41e82d5d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/commits/d806733f3065bae55a553861aef934199a8227ad","verification":{"payload":"tree 85ea970ad589dc4e0de9d2e7b104243a41e82d5d\nparent 43cc59a6e895975e80ce2278aa6bb2b524d599cb\nauthor David Arce <davidarce2915@gmail.com> 1778363678 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778363678 +0200\n\nfix(workflows/sdd): align OpenCode orchestrator on Task() + WORKFLOW_SUBAGENT_ADVISOR (#56)\n\n* fix(workflows/sdd): align OpenCode orchestrator on Task() syntax + WORKFLOW_SUBAGENT_ADVISOR placeholder\n\nThe OpenCode orchestrator received contradictory invocation instructions\nbecause REGISTRY.opencode.md described `@<sub-agent>` natural-language\nmentions while ORCHESTRATOR.opencode.md (correctly) used `Task()`. The\ntwo blocks are concatenated into the synthesised orchestrator prompt,\nso the model saw both syntaxes and stalled deciding between them.\n\nIndependently, `_shared/advisor-templates.md` hardcoded\n`subagent_type: ''general-purpose''` for both the parallel and the\nsequential templates. The catalog already declares an `sdd-advisor`\nrole in `workflow.yaml`, and `{WORKFLOW_SUBAGENT_ADVISOR}` is the\nplaceholder DevRune resolves at install time — so the templates were\npointing at a non-existent agent for OpenCode (which exposes only the\nagents declared in `opencode.json`).\n\nChanges:\n- REGISTRY.opencode.md — replace `@<sub-agent>` / `@sdd-{phase}` with\n  `Task(subagent_type: ''{WORKFLOW_SUBAGENT_<PHASE>}'', ...)`. Aligns\n  with ORCHESTRATOR.opencode.md and removes the contradiction.\n- _shared/advisor-templates.md — swap `''general-purpose''` for\n  `''{WORKFLOW_SUBAGENT_ADVISOR}''` on both templates. Generic file is\n  still consumed by Claude/Factory; placeholder resolves to the\n  agent name declared in `workflow.yaml` per renderer.\n- _shared/advisor-templates.opencode.md (NEW) — OpenCode-only variant\n  with just the Sequential template + Plan Re-entry template, no\n  `model:` or `run_in_background:` fields (OpenCode resolves model\n  from the agent definition in opencode.json). Renderer renames it\n  to `advisor-templates.md` and suppresses the generic for OpenCode\n  installs, matching the existing pattern for `launch-templates`.\n\n* fix(workflows/sdd): drop redundant prose for OpenCode orchestrator\n\nThree follow-ups from PR #56 review — the agent already knows it is the\nsdd-orchestrator, already knows OpenCode''s run_in_background limitation,\nand already knows model is sourced from opencode.json. Saying so wastes\nprompt budget.\n\n- REGISTRY.opencode.md \"How to Start\": drop the \"you ARE the orchestrator\"\n  sentence; renumber from 1.\n- REGISTRY.opencode.md \"Compaction Recovery\": drop the same self-identity\n  step; move recovery.md path to the preamble; renumber from 1.\n- advisor-templates.opencode.md: drop the OpenCode-constraint callout and\n  the \"do not pass model:\" callout. The remaining Task() snippet shows\n  the correct shape on its own.\n\n* fix(workflows/sdd): drop OpenCode self-reference in advisor-templates header\n\nPR #56 follow-up: the file is renamed to advisor-templates.md at install\ntime, so ''(OpenCode)'' in the H1 and the ''OpenCode-only file'' HTML comment\nboth lose meaning in the materialised workspace. Removed both, plus the\nSYNC WITH note (catalog-maintainer concern, belongs in commit history /\ndocs not in the runtime artifact).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp/60eCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEl8QAJR1Ms4wigLcEaAZMfuIkxsD\n+PQNrGMK8nAWWkyChOBawmmgTFWFgmUYFCLhekR+gW43uDFLV2ZYOMtkfvXB+uke\n6MnpUn1KFs0ObeYHQ6kmfs6J03qv2JhpwOu7c97pvI7bHz38HWto23wEbcveZ1fL\nimNtFr78W82/xHu09mic/ErGZwLoL2aapYAikpJt+QU0Hou99ngzZg6qvL7r63MS\nG+dLlBhl4WZej2IBFQWHoFKsCgmKHrbv8mYI8HBe6rkzoJ9NuciKVZVBSYy6LTwv\nCEUgyb1HMxIsOHE9M0F/MADKvE+n83Ro/q0BgtCsgFKAxyehd4i9KB42NuQdAvaM\nw5pmlCGrXqYhYLNSGd669URYX4CubcSbpDkIECDl28TdJoHQv2nyKjCEVMdSZZqy\nF/RfTJXMuBb1mYIEcTk0u0dS04c0Wvz1vu+MvwmLWOhCFE7q7sVT1rl2QS23yMFg\nnA+LbvwD5nMgksnOmOO+qE9jV1HLtSuUv2Sd3P59eaaE6QdUsv0dBZJhN4ohH6gm\n3lkCWEivV5qjQG+OWOyku6sIj3PmM9+xhlekDxUpyX1JvQ+BgF8AdDb+5KW4oPck\n1nkTFWSi/YMVPtbJEI4pSCVwq0/iFuThqblmc6QA0I86nSDvMFyg8MljpoOJ3tMD\n65bJr0k1vqqavyn4Kqlh\n=Lvio\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-09T21:54:39Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commit/d806733f3065bae55a553861aef93419