nts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/8e0b3437cb634e3a9a4ee32710f676db459ef146/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-09T18:57:10Z","email":"davidarce2915@gmail.com","name":"David Arce"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-09T18:57:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(workflows/sdd)!: per-agent role models, drop dead fields, section comments (#54)\n\n* feat(workflows/sdd)!: per-agent role models, drop dead fields, section comments\n\nSchema\n------\n- roles[].models is now required for kind: subagent — a map keyed by agent\n  name (claude, opencode, copilot) with the model alias each agent''s\n  renderer expects:\n    - claude:   short tier names (haiku, sonnet, opus)\n    - opencode: short tier names or fully-qualified provider/model strings\n    - copilot:  VS Code display names verbatim (e.g. \"Claude Sonnet 4.6\")\n  DevRune seeds the TUI model-selection step from these defaults.\n- roles[].model (single string) is removed.\n\nSkills\n------\n- Add git-commit and git-pull-request to components.skills. They are core\n  closures of the SDD flow but only `components.skills` triggers install\n  (decisionRules / invocationControls / permissions never did).\n\nCleanup\n-------\n- Drop components.decisionRules and components.invocationControls — both\n  are unused by DevRune (zero consumers in cli, tui, materialize, recommend,\n  parse; only present in the round-trip yaml test).\n- Reorganise inline comments into per-section headers so contributors can\n  see at a glance what each block is and how DevRune consumes it.\n\nBumps metadata.version 1.0.0 -> 1.1.0. Requires DevRune with the matching\nWorkflowRole.Models support (PR davidarce/DevRune#XX).\n\nCloses #53\n\n* review(workflows/sdd): drop inline skill comments, use canonical opencode IDs\n\nAddresses PR #54 review comments:\n- Remove per-skill inline comments (write-a-prd / git-commit / git-pull-request);\n  the section header already explains the two-pass resolver.\n- Use explicit github-copilot/<id> format for opencode model defaults instead of\n  short tier names. The resolveOpenCodeModel resolver still accepts shorts but\n  the canonical form is more self-documenting and works for any provider.\n- Update the section comment to recommend the explicit form.","tree":{"sha":"3e0eee65d14da52d2cdc9169eaedbc1eca433bb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/trees/3e0eee65d14da52d2cdc9169eaedbc1eca433bb5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/commits/8e0b3437cb634e3a9a4ee32710f676db459ef146","verification":{"payload":"tree 3e0eee65d14da52d2cdc9169eaedbc1eca433bb5\nparent 1e0c659d92974229827068312b514f23f69ef325\nauthor David Arce <davidarce2915@gmail.com> 1778353030 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778353030 +0200\n\nfix(workflows/sdd)!: per-agent role models, drop dead fields, section comments (#54)\n\n* feat(workflows/sdd)!: per-agent role models, drop dead fields, section comments\n\nSchema\n------\n- roles[].models is now required for kind: subagent — a map keyed by agent\n  name (claude, opencode, copilot) with the model alias each agent''s\n  renderer expects:\n    - claude:   short tier names (haiku, sonnet, opus)\n    - opencode: short tier names or fully-qualified provider/model strings\n    - copilot:  VS Code display names verbatim (e.g. \"Claude Sonnet 4.6\")\n  DevRune seeds the TUI model-selection step from these defaults.\n- roles[].model (single string) is removed.\n\nSkills\n------\n- Add git-commit and git-pull-request to components.skills. They are core\n  closures of the SDD flow but only `components.skills` triggers install\n  (decisionRules / invocationControls / permissions never did).\n\nCleanup\n-------\n- Drop components.decisionRules and components.invocationControls — both\n  are unused by DevRune (zero consumers in cli, tui, materialize, recommend,\n  parse; only present in the round-trip yaml test).\n- Reorganise inline comments into per-section headers so contributors can\n  see at a glance what each block is and how DevRune consumes it.\n\nBumps metadata.version 1.0.0 -> 1.1.0. Requires DevRune with the matching\nWorkflowRole.Models support (PR davidarce/DevRune#XX).\n\nCloses #53\n\n* review(workflows/sdd): drop inline skill comments, use canonical opencode IDs\n\nAddresses PR #54 review comments:\n- Remove per-skill inline comments (write-a-prd / git-commit / git-pull-request);\n  the section header already explains the two-pass resolver.\n- Use explicit github-copilot/<id> format for opencode model defaults instead of\n  short tier names. The resolveOpenCodeModel resolver still accepts shorts but\n  the canonical form is more self-documenting and works for any provider.\n- Update the section comment to recommend the explicit form.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp/4OGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+s8QAJs6YQT3JNdoJURfxGIhMWXx\n2wZfmIXiTXyMva5/wtaQgwk43iOvQnlbIk8Tb13VR3farpo/TQsH2g5nnWmK9aJo\nKbXxPAGjYp4hxfsiz2qw3+Cx3fIoSXPrdix9pld4iFlDZu9310ujtH1xb3dHGVQS\nZ8DUIQk9dQyiQV/uYVlfJ+M4xTcPxf8DrZVlVD56sZCy/waq7RQo5tPMMajHNSq2\nTJqM/QG7mpfr4XbCDanRU2P0T5wiyNa2qJ5QGvXVbY8fwFfif4bDWGlgLPGOKlyQ\nzjDxVfPC+Z6BbHNoD/eaOg1wTpmPr2dBVxENlEGrWekdL0qnMuBG3zWJKzxYvJmA\n3gzyO6jSPolf+qWpCYNMFdvk17fHbIdMnO4xc7TiudU/qcpGdW2hBRd8z8Um/aKB\n+lSRbUG6Ka8haQPcv00vq6fcIGRoFJeCArk4o+ZXV+JQ/VGNqpmRuVOVj1/h9GG3\nfyUVIvJMzziIN2lUWWmhE6mOnK5Of+M1onP5Fmgq0hQTmbLMF3TAUTHXezzilEfT\nAgD8CZhMCLvZqYZpzoxNjGlq4bsrJwzyfIHujMLEjRdqpZ//vHMu1AOiKi9AMEM+\nGKhZnCa1