"https://github.com/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commit/1e0c659d92974229827068312b514f23f69ef325","node_id":"C_kwDORwxuadoAKDFlMGM2NTlkOTI5NzQyMjk4MjcwNjgzMTJiNTE0ZjIzZjY5ZWYzMjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commit/d62aeda854144f95a132d69469935b3118a01311","sha":"d62aeda854144f95a132d69469935b3118a01311","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/d62aeda854144f95a132d69469935b3118a01311"}],"sha":"1e0c659d92974229827068312b514f23f69ef325","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/1e0c659d92974229827068312b514f23f69ef325"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13999850?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce","id":13999850,"login":"davidarce","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTk5ODUw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/d62aeda854144f95a132d69469935b3118a01311/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-06T08:14:22Z","email":"davidarce2915@gmail.com","name":"David Arce"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-06T08:14:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(sdd): tighten adviser coverage, review-ok auto-flow (#49) (#51)\n\n* feat(sdd): tighten adviser coverage, review-ok auto-flow (#49)\n\nThree workflow autonomy improvements to reduce orchestrator interruptions\nand ensure the adviser registry is actually used:\n\n- Adviser coverage gate: sdd-plan paso 5 now requires advisers whose\n  described domain overlaps the plan''s contracts/tasks; Detail Quality\n  Gate rejects boilerplate skip rationales. Rule is semantic against\n  each adviser''s `description` frontmatter, not tech-specific keywords.\n\n- Skill-in-host handoff (write-a-prd Self-Check): the skill must not\n  emit handoff narration after persisting the PRD; the host''s main loop\n  resumes immediately. One self-contained bullet, no shared file.\n\n- Review ok = natural workflow completion: rewritten Post-Review Fix\n  Cycle in all 4 ORCHESTRATOR variants. ok auto-commits, auto-PRs, and\n  marks the workflow COMPLETED with no asks. commit/PR failures ask\n  Retry / Abort symmetrically. No partial-success terminal — only\n  COMPLETED and ABORTED.\n\n- PRD gate auto-continue: step 4 in all 4 variants now states the\n  orchestrator auto-launches explore immediately when write-a-prd\n  returns — no ask, no narration, no wait.\n\n- state.yaml schema extension (_shared/persistence-contract.md): adds\n  optional commit_completed, commit_sha, awaiting_user_decision fields\n  with documented Recovery Semantics so the auto-flow is safe across\n  compaction boundaries.\n\narchitect-advisor consulted during planning (round 1):\n- Skill-handoff contract: dropped shared file (overengineering per\n  user); kept self-contained Self-Check bullet.\n- PR failure path: drop \"Skip PR (mark COMPLETED)\" — symmetric Retry/\n  Abort preserves clean two-terminal lifecycle.\n\nAll wording tech-agnostic. All per-agent variants updated consistently.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(sdd): drop redundant write-a-prd handoff bullet and branch defensive note\n\nPost-review feedback on PR #51:\n\n- write-a-prd Self-Check: remove the handoff-narration bullet. Fix 5\n  (PRD gate step 4) already states the orchestrator auto-launches\n  explore when this skill returns. The rule lives in the host, not\n  inside the skill itself.\n\n- Post-Review Fix Cycle (3 ORCHESTRATOR variants): remove the trailing\n  defensive note about branch already being set up at workflow start.\n  The initial step enforces it; restating it here adds noise. If the\n  initial step fails, that is a separate problem.\n\nORCHESTRATOR.opencode.md had no such clause — no change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fc2abb938527722619a8ec342e78799a61e940f6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/trees/fc2abb938527722619a8ec342e78799a61e940f6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/commits/d62aeda854144f95a132d69469935b3118a01311","verification":{"payload":"tree fc2abb938527722619a8ec342e78799a61e940f6\nparent a204cd64b0c1cfe2e9ff5da24b62c36df08028d2\nauthor David Arce <davidarce2915@gmail.com> 1778055262 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1778055262 +0200\n\nfeat(sdd): tighten adviser coverage, review-ok auto-flow (#49) (#51)\n\n* feat(sdd): tighten adviser coverage, review-ok auto-flow (#49)\n\nThree workflow autonomy improvements to reduce orchestrator interruptions\nand ensure the adviser registry is actually used:\n\n- Adviser coverage gate: sdd-plan paso 5 now requires advisers whose\n  described domain overlaps the plan''s contracts/tasks; Detail Quality\n  Gate rejects boilerplate skip rationales. Rule is semantic against\n  each adviser''s `description` frontmatter, not tech-specific keywords.\n\n- Skill-in-host handoff (write-a-prd Self-Check): the skill must not\n  emit handoff narration after persisting the PRD; the host''s main loop\n  resumes immediately. One self-contained bullet, no shared file.\n\n- Review ok = natural workflow completion: rewritten Post-Review Fix\n  Cycle in all 4 ORCHESTRATOR variants. ok auto-commits, auto-PRs, and\n  marks the workflow COMPLETED with no asks. commit/PR failures ask\n  Retry / Abort symmetrically. No partial-success terminal — only\n  COMPLETED and ABORTED.\n\n- PRD gate auto-continue: step 4 in all 4 variants now states the\n  orchestrator auto-launches explore immediately when write-a-prd\n  returns — no ask, no narration, no wait.\n\n- state.yaml schema extension (_shared/persistence-contract.md): adds\n  optional commit_completed, commit_sha, awaiting_user_decision fields\n  with documented Recovery Semantics so the auto-flow is safe across\n  compaction boundaries.\n\narchitect-advisor consulted during planning (round 1):\n- Skill-handoff contract: dropped shared file (overengineering per\n  user); kept self-contained Self-Check bullet.\n- PR failure path: drop \"Skip PR (mark COMPLETED)\" — symmetric Retry/\n  Abort preserves clean two-terminal lifecycle.\n\nAll wording tech-agnostic. All per-agent variants updated consistently.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor(sdd): drop redundant write-a-prd handoff bullet and branch defensive note\n\nPost-review feedback on PR #51:\n\n- write-a-prd Self-Check: remove the handoff-narration bullet. Fix 5\n  (PRD gate step 4) already states the orchestrator auto-launches\n  explore when this skill returns. The rule lives in the host, not\n  inside the skill itself.\n\n- Post-Review Fix Cycle (3 ORCHESTRATOR variants): remove the trailing\n  defensive note about branch already being set up at workflow start.\n  The initial step enforces it; restating it here adds noise. If the\n  initial step fails, that is a separate problem.\n\nORCHESTRATOR.opencode.md had no such clause — no change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE--