users/davidarce/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/b57cf03961854584c1596fd5437269e75b28dd9c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T10:56:47Z","email":"davidarce2915@gmail.com","name":"David Arce"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T10:56:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(sdd): include write-a-prd as workflow dependency (#47)\n\nSDD''s PRD gate (Step 1 in ORCHESTRATOR) invokes Skill(\"write-a-prd\")\nat workflow start. Until now this dependency lived implicitly in each\nuser''s devrune.yaml manual select — easy to forget, hard to discover.\n\nThe DevRune renderer now resolves components.skills entries against the\ncatalog top level (devrune-starter-catalog#issue-link in DevRune#65),\nso listing write-a-prd here pulls it in automatically when SDD is\ninstalled: catalog/skills/write-a-prd/SKILL.md materialises into the\nagent workspace alongside the SDD phase skills.\n\nAlso adds Skill(write-a-prd) to the workflow''s permissions so the\norchestrator can call it without the user having to grant a one-off\npermission.\n\nRequires devrune#65 to be merged for catalog-level resolution to work\non a fresh install. Pre-merge installs that already have write-a-prd\nin their devrune.yaml select keep working unchanged.","tree":{"sha":"cc58d00d0f26cd8fc1e2c928e58520c31bf9a32d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/trees/cc58d00d0f26cd8fc1e2c928e58520c31bf9a32d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/commits/b57cf03961854584c1596fd5437269e75b28dd9c","verification":{"payload":"tree cc58d00d0f26cd8fc1e2c928e58520c31bf9a32d\nparent aa3861f3ec1610c01f7b007ed3ecf6649d50eed5\nauthor David Arce <davidarce2915@gmail.com> 1777978607 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777978607 +0200\n\nfeat(sdd): include write-a-prd as workflow dependency (#47)\n\nSDD''s PRD gate (Step 1 in ORCHESTRATOR) invokes Skill(\"write-a-prd\")\nat workflow start. Until now this dependency lived implicitly in each\nuser''s devrune.yaml manual select — easy to forget, hard to discover.\n\nThe DevRune renderer now resolves components.skills entries against the\ncatalog top level (devrune-starter-catalog#issue-link in DevRune#65),\nso listing write-a-prd here pulls it in automatically when SDD is\ninstalled: catalog/skills/write-a-prd/SKILL.md materialises into the\nagent workspace alongside the SDD phase skills.\n\nAlso adds Skill(write-a-prd) to the workflow''s permissions so the\norchestrator can call it without the user having to grant a one-off\npermission.\n\nRequires devrune#65 to be merged for catalog-level resolution to work\non a fresh install. Pre-merge installs that already have write-a-prd\nin their devrune.yaml select keep working unchanged.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp+czvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAXAAQACdX59q83Eb3d4EwdKPqn40k\n0besr522DGkvxpMLTpBLgMKIlIwFHT3XSKPcnSNGj9BWAwb4pDzhIvLBnD0pPjHY\nIqLeOYL6GMN8zPbLc5KSxqexdv5lL1ug/xtK+Tqc7Culb+S2lB2A8azaOgVF35b0\nvyqvY70Z6SzNReq32uEtCY8ytSsAZBfa3kTFfOwYlyJE8OIwCLwXNXkjPBAnW5n3\nBd78xkpsxvgEh+/T0Qmq8qP+blWItEXF9pF3BcHgQR22GqHRHsDFY06GwAC6RuQ5\nZ0fk4IcUtdqzoN2VGKNw+h/FInsKq3MzPpkcR+4VSgZm2WB3BdzlVSoX5K884Rsb\nrfHYqDmt9/4+Bc0uDhEsqnVFRWeji2pGWd8sg4+fu5kTqqQQxzdhoG2VG7ciwEyy\n+hKHMj7yseXkKuTG8SGFWrT/sxowIfBfrUxFqKcJfEbfA5hy45mDbgS+PTLnuVLf\nlqYqi0FExx11bJDEr21gvdncTcIZNDytPG5Hz8SsuZfAf479R3ctzjHrYKGkcSgO\nee9oAfHcJhFA8r/luYFTyvy0Ni6tMb160vPTSieqa12SP6ry/LHGiAzZW/4TdgBX\nPlJ5xOYhNALaUAof4zmFUblvJGUWAmNocnZnEsRkKZphiLIk2nEXrx2eaMyC24Tk\n2E86Wv4g1QcePj0u4x1i\n=7kL5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-05T10:56:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commit/b57cf03961854584c1596fd5437269e75b28dd9c","node_id":"C_kwDORwxuadoAKGI1N2NmMDM5NjE4NTQ1ODRjMTU5NmZkNTQzNzI2OWU3NWIyOGRkOWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commit/aa3861f3ec1610c01f7b007ed3ecf6649d50eed5","sha":"aa3861f3ec1610c01f7b007ed3ecf6649d50eed5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/aa3861f3ec1610c01f7b007ed3ecf6649d50eed5"}],"sha":"b57cf03961854584c1596fd5437269e75b28dd9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/b57cf03961854584c1596fd5437269e75b28dd9c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13999850?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce","id":13999850,"login":"davidarce","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTk5ODUw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/aa3861f3ec1610c01f7b007ed3ecf6649d50eed5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-05T09:53:28Z","email":"davidarce2915@gmail.com","name":"David Arce"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-05T09:53:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"sdd: workflow hardening — envelope trust, output discipline, branch safety (#46)\n\n* refactor(sdd): pre-commit gate + trust envelope gates in orchestrator\n\nTwo related orchestrator hardenings, applied across all four\nORCHESTRATOR variants (md, claude, copilot, opencode):\n\n- **Pre-Commit Gate** (issue #45-1): before delegating to git-commit,\n  validate the current branch fits {change-name}. Branch is fit when\n  its slug matches change-name OR has zero commits ahead of base.\n  Otherwise AskUserQuestion offers Create new feature branch /\n  Commit anyway / Abort. Validation lives in the orchestrator —\n  git-commit stays agnostic for standalone use.\n\n- **Trust the envelope** (issue #45-12): explicit Post-Phase Protocol\n  rule that the orchestrator MUST NOT re-run build/test/lint/vet after\n  a sub-agent envelope returns status: ok with a Gates: line. The\n  implementer contract already covers those signals; double-verifying\n  burns tokens and time. Manual validation only kicks in on warning\n  or failed envelopes, and only on the flagged signals.\n\n* refactor(sdd): plan SELF-CHECKS PRD coverage before crit (issue #45-3)\n\nWhen .sdd/{change}/prd.md exists, sdd-plan''s Detail Quality Gate now\nwalks the PRD top-to-bottom and verifies each User Story / requirement\nmaps to at least one TXXX task in the plan. The mapping is recorded\nin `## 4. Clarifications`. Self-Check echoes the requirement at the\nend of the flow as a redundant guard.\n\nCatches gaps where the reviewer would have surfaced critical issues\nbecause the plan didn''t cover all PRD User Stories — moves the find\nfrom review-time (where the fix means re-implementing) to plan-time\n(where it''s a small task addition).\n\n* refactor(sdd): crit daemon pre-flight + auto-retry (issue #45-5)\n\nTwo-part hardening of the Crit Plan Review Protocol:\n\n- **Pre-flight** before launching crit: scan for and kill any stale\n  daemon matching `crit plan.*{change}`. Stale daemons from a prior\n  round were the root cause of the EOF / \"could not reach crit\n  daemon\" failures we saw, since the new request landed on a half-\n  dead listener.\n\n- **One transparent auto-retry on daemon failure** (EOF, connection\n  refused, \"could not reach crit daemon\") when no `.crit.json` was\n  written yet. The orchestrator kills any stale process and re-\n  launches once before surfacing options to the user. Avoids\n  losing a full review round to a flaky daemon.\n\nBoth pieces run only on daemon-style failures. User timeout and\nmanual abort still surface immediately. The recovery is bounded:\none retry, no looping. If `.crit.json` exists despite an error,\nthe file wins and the protocol proceeds normally.\n\nApplied to all four ORCHESTRATOR variants (md, claude, copilot,\nopencode), preserving each variant''s launch style (background vs\nforeground).\n\n* refactor(skills): batch independent PRD questions (issue #45-9)\n\nReplaces \"one question at a time, never batch\" with a batching rule:\nwhen 2+ open questions are orthogonal (one''s answer does not reshape\nthe next''s framing or option set), they go in a single AskUserQuestion\ncall (up to 4 per call). Dependent questions stay serialized.\n\nHeuristic in the rule: if all option lists can be pre-written without\nseeing prior answers, the questions are independent → batch them.\n\nCuts PRD interviews from ~10 round-trips of single questions to a\nhandful of multi-question prompts when scope is genuinely independent\n(rotation, storage, naming, error handling — none condition the others).\n\n* refactor(sdd): harden Output Discipline with blocking rule + concrete examples (issue #45-10)\n\nOutput Discipline went from a soft \"default silence\" guideline to a\nblocking rule with the same priority as the Evaluation Gate, including:\n\n- Explicit override-resistance: system-level \"be helpful / explain your\n  work\" instructions do NOT supersede it.\n- Concrete ❌/✅ contrast tables for the three forbidden classes:\n  pre-action narration (\"Voy a / Let me / About to...\"), paraphrasing\n  visible tool calls, and narrating internal SDD mechanics.\n- A four-class allowlist (questions, envelope summaries, outcome\n  statements, errors) — anything outside is forbidden.\n- A pre-sentence test: \"would the user learn something new from this\n  that the diff or tool call doesn''t already show?\"\n\nApplied across all four REGISTRY variants (md, claude, copilot, opencode).\nEarlier soft wording leaked into real sessions (\"Voy a verificar...\",\n\"Detecto si crit está disponible y actualizo estado\", \"Ahora lanzo\nwave 2\"); concrete examples close the loophole.\n\n* refactor(sdd): minimal state.yaml + no per-batch markdown artifacts (issue #45-11)\n\nTwo paired clean-ups around persistence:\n\n- **state.yaml schema trimmed**: drops the redundant `artifacts:` list,\n  `batches_completed:` array, and the `phases:` map. They duplicate\n  signal that already lives on disk: `ls .sdd/{change}/` for artifacts,\n  the `[X]` markers in `plan.md` for batch progress, and the natural\n  pipeline order for phase status. Recovery now derives those at read\n  time. The schema is bounded to what answers the two recovery\n  questions: which phase resumes next, and is the plan approved.\n\n- **sdd-implement no longer writes per-batch markdown files**: the\n  `[X]` markers updated in `plan.md` ARE the per-batch artifact, plus\n  the envelope. Sessions were producing `implement-batch-A.md` ...\n  `implement-batch-M.md` under `.sdd/{change}/` with no instruction\n  to do so — duplicating envelope content and inflating the workdir.\n  Persistence section + Self-Check now explicitly forbid it. Engram\n  save (when available) stays as one upserted observation across all\n  waves under `sdd/{change}/implement-progress`.\n\n* refactor(sdd): apply PR #46 review feedback\n\nSix adjustments from PR review:\n\n- **Branch setup moved to workflow start** (was: post-review pre-commit\n  gate). The orchestrator now creates `.sdd/{change}/` AND ensures a\n  fitting branch (`feat/`, `fix/`, `refactor/`, `chore/`, `docs/`)\n  during First Sub-Agent of a New Workflow, deriving the type from\n  the user prompt or bound ticket and asking only when unclear. Resume\n  case skips this step entirely. The post-review gate is removed —\n  branch state set at start is final, mid-workflow changes are\n  deliberate user choices.\n\n- **Output Discipline examples in English only**. The ❌/✅ tables\n  dropped Spanish examples (\"Voy a verificar...\", \"Auto-transición a\n  plan\", etc.) — instructions stay in English regardless of which\n  language the agent ends up speaking.\n\n- **Trust-envelope rule generalized**. No more `go build` / `go test` /\n  `go vet` mentions — the rule now reads \"any verification command\n  (build / test / lint / format / type-check — whatever the project\n  uses)\". SDD is stack-agnostic.\n\n- **Crit auto-retry is silent**. Removed the \"Crit daemon dropped —\n  retrying once\" user-facing message. The orchestrator retries\n  transparently and only surfaces options if the retry also fails.\n\n- **write-a-prd batching example abstracted**. Dropped the concrete\n  \"backups + menu label + rotation\" example — instructions stay\n  feature-agnostic.\n\n- **sdd-implement persistence rule generalized**. \"Don''t write\n  implement-batch-{id}.md\" became \"don''t create or modify any\n  artifact under `.sdd/{change}/` other than the [X] updates to\n  plan.md.\" The principle, not the symptom.","tree":{"sha":"0fe956ab5b999107b3790102d67094213f418706","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/trees/0fe956ab5b999107b3790102d67094213f418706"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/commits/aa3861f3ec1610c01f7b007ed3ecf6649d50eed5","verification":{"payload":"tree 0fe956ab5b999107b3790102d67094213f418706\nparent 8b1a5a91336e94ea512491978ac9e5174378d4bd\nauthor David Arce <davidarce2915@gmail.com> 1777974808 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777974808 +0200\n\nsdd: workflow hardening — envelope trust, output discipline, branch safety (#46)\n\n* refactor(sdd): pre-commit gate + trust envelope gates in orchestrator\n\nTwo related orchestrator hardenings, applied across all four\nORCHESTRATOR variants (md, claude, copilot, opencode):\n\n- **Pre-Commit Gate** (issue #45-1): before delegating to git-commit,\n  validate the current branch fits {change-name}. Branch is fit when\n  its slug matches change-name OR has zero commits ahead of base.\n  Otherwise AskUserQuestion offers Create new feature branch /\n  Commit anyway / Abort. Validation lives in the orchestrator —\n  git-commit stays agnostic for standalone use.\n\n- **Trust the envelope** (issue #45-12): explicit Post-Phase Protocol\n  rule that the orchestrator MUST NOT re-run build/test/lint/vet after\n  a sub-agent envelope returns status: ok with a Gates: line. The\n  implementer contract already covers those signals; double-verifying\n  burns tokens and time. Manual validation only kicks in on warning\n  or failed envelopes, and only on the flagged signals.\n\n* refactor(sdd): plan SELF-CHECKS PRD coverage before crit (issue #45-3)\n\nWhen .sdd/{change}/prd.md exists, sdd-plan''s Detail Quality Gate now\nwalks the PRD top-to-bottom and verifies each User Story / requirement\nmaps to at least one TXXX task in the plan. The mapping is recorded\nin `## 4. Clarifications`. Self-Check echoes the requirement at the\nend of the flow as a redundant guard.\n\nCatches gaps where the reviewer would have surfaced critical issues\nbecause the plan didn''t cover all PRD User Stories — moves the find\nfrom review-time (where the fix means re-implementing) to plan-time\n(where it''s a small task addition).\n\n* refactor(sdd): crit daemon pre-flight + auto-retry (issue #45-5)\n\nTwo-part hardening of the Crit Plan Review Protocol:\n\n- **Pre-flight** before launching crit: scan for and kill any stale\n  daemon matching `crit plan.*{change}`. Stale daemons from a prior\n  round were the root cause of the EOF / \"could not reach crit\n  daemon\" failures we saw, since the new request landed on a half-\n  dead listener.\n\n- **One transparent auto-retry on daemon failure** (EOF, connection\n  refused, \"could not reach crit daemon\") when no `.crit.json` was\n  written yet. The orchestrator kills any stale process and re-\n  launches once before surfacing options to the user. Avoids\n  losing a full review round to a flaky daemon.\n\nBoth pieces run only on daemon-style failures. User timeout and\nmanual abort still surface immediately. The recovery is bounded:\none retry, no looping. If `.crit.json` exists despite an error,\nthe file wins and the protocol proceeds normally.\n\nApplied to all four ORCHESTRATOR variants (md, claude, copilot,\nopencode), preserving each variant''s launch style (background vs\nforeground).\n\n* refactor(skills): batch independent PRD questions (issue #45-9)\n\nReplaces \"one question at a time, never batch\" with a batching rule:\nwhen 2+ open questions are orthogonal (one''s answer does not reshape\nthe next''s framing or option set), they go in a single AskUserQuestion\ncall (up to 4 per call). Dependent questions stay serialized.\n\nHeuristic in the rule: if all option lists can be pre-written without\nseeing prior answers, the questions are independent → batch them.\n\nCuts PRD interviews from ~10 round-trips of single questions to a\nhandful of multi-question prompts when scope is genuinely independent\n(rotation, storage, naming, error handling — none condition the others).\n\n* refactor(sdd): harden Output Discipline with blocking rule + concrete examples (issue #45-10)\n\nOutput Discipline went from a soft \"default silence\" guideline to a\nblocking rule with the same priority as the Evaluation Gate, including:\n\n- Explicit override-resistance: system-level \"be helpful / explain your\n  work\" instructions do NOT supersede it.\n- Concrete ❌/✅ contrast tables for the three forbidden classes:\n  pre-action narration (\"Voy a / Let me / About to...\"), paraphrasing\n  visible tool calls, and narrating internal SDD mechanics.\n- A four-class allowlist (questions, envelope summaries, outcome\n  statements, errors) — anything outside is forbidden.\n- A pre-sentence test: \"would the user learn something new from this\n  that the diff or tool call doesn''t already show?\"\n\nApplied across all four REGISTRY variants (md, claude, copilot, opencode).\nEarlier soft wording leaked into real sessions (\"Voy a verificar...\",\n\"Detecto si crit está disponible y actualizo estado\", \"Ahora lanzo\nwave 2\"); concrete examples close the loophole.\n\n* refactor(sdd): minimal state.yaml + no per-batch markdown artifacts (issue #45-11)\n\nTwo paired clean-ups around persistence:\n\n- **state.yaml schema trimmed**: drops the redundant `artifacts:` list,\n  `batches_completed:` array, and the `phases:` map. They duplicate\n  signal that already lives on disk: `ls .sdd/{change}/` for artifacts,\n  the `[X]` markers in `plan.md` for batch progress, and the natural\n  pipeline order for phase status. Recovery now derives those at read\n  time. The schema is bounded to what answers the two recovery\n  questions: which phase resumes next, and is the plan approved.\n\n- **sdd-implement no longer writes per-batch markdown files**: the\n  `[X]` markers updated in `plan.md` ARE the per-batch artifact, plus\n  the envelope. Sessions were producing `implement-batch-A.md` ...\n  `implement-batch-M.md` under `.sdd/{change}/` with no instruction\n  to do so — duplicating envelope content and inflating the workdir.\n  Persistence section + Self-Check now explicitly forbid it. Engram\n  save (when available) stays as one upserted observation across all\n  waves under `sdd/{change}/implement-progress`.\n\n* refactor(sdd): apply PR #46 review feedback\n\nSix adjustments from PR review:\n\n- **Branch setup moved to workflow start** (was: post-review pre-commit\n  gate). The orchestrator now creates `.sdd/{change}/` AND ensures a\n  fitting branch (`feat/`, `fix/`, `refactor/`, `chore/`, `docs/`)\n  during First Sub-Agent of a New Workflow, deriving the type from\n  the user prompt or bound ticket and asking only when unclear. Resume\n  case skips this step entirely. The post-review gate is removed —\n  branch state set at start is final, mid-workflow changes are\n  deliberate user choices.\n\n- **Output Discipline examples in English only**. The ❌/✅ tables\n  dropped Spanish examples (\"Voy a verificar...\", \"Auto-transición a\n  plan\", etc.) — instructions stay in English regardless of which\n  language the agent ends up speaking.\n\n- **Trust-envelope rule generalized**. No more `go build` / `go test` /\n  `go vet` mentions — the rule now reads \"any verification command\n  (build / test / lint / format / type-check — whatever the project\n  uses)\". SDD is stack-agnostic.\n\n- **Crit auto-retry is silent**. Removed the \"Crit daemon dropped —\n  retrying once\" user-facing message. The orchestrator retries\n  transparently and only surfaces options if the retry also fails.\n\n- **write-a-prd batching example abstracted**. Dropped the concrete\n  \"backups + menu label + rotation\" example — instructions stay\n  feature-agnostic.\n\n- **sdd-implement persistence rule generalized**. \"Don''t write\n  implement-batch-{id}.md\" became \"don''t create or modify any\n  artifact under `.sdd/{change}/` other than the [X] updates to\n  plan.md.\" The principle, not the symptom.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp+b4YCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4qcQAFZp0/jptScBj75YRV1MTB5m\n1TtDLBta2XROtNT3qLVaCCgu97Q2kyeNVFL0gmGpLKuVSdD5n9nfkml4rQeHuPsD\nZ5gPalvm2ets2cn1Jb5hj6rrDIDiKiKk9GSb3g7dpkVyDGdS1/9LwiQMWxqWOfRn\ncApIL7EpMviwEWxdNqHVMnvO7+4lRz6MSWBuxhtl5VbFz6z6rMQRtpUmmGoFJeNK\nsOMJGvQCLbo57++0UD21MTKHAkZhlIGcpPfE5CbzqdT8XoBsKR76RVlPizH8vh2o\nQEVuSs+fS3QmCAX0i49t7QIvKJ+tETZmj+cIcqaoAfjW98nOGbRrGUC+1G+OmNLV\n3VO8BHwfHC9Ir3IP1xAKcWlzi8U7dzL1CnpvyenkuunNabRwwCvKX76If5heuODv\nfQoauPZyPMefRsm/ZAsEpR+0KC7x1fzI7ss0FZ6Y83hKJgjB2vITgVwa2WNej0pW\nzL+N+PXGP4O0OFEbleSRx33ERgoE9MxZeuaM0+quKMReHuQEuQnmiLvSLVZA3d2U\ngCyMMnnkmG1FmeWjE3lSIUmk7pf/XFMEpoBYnWpMauCYYT8Ks+9gIlEXMD/unBfm\nwCr/IOjG+qZkTjmJc0v8WJkSQ/ooG+wLmZxAs6//vag+5dpogF6y+T12Zc5IRFPP\nnyO5SZJx5U+ZDa3F68xy\n=Lld3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-05T09:53:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web