ist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commit/61e67654c80c36dff5a4ea8ecbe2998ee7df465a","node_id":"C_kwDORwxuadoAKDYxZTY3NjU0YzgwYzM2ZGZmNWE0ZWE4ZWNiZTI5OThlZTdkZjQ2NWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commit/8a0752b447c2fcc1580afdc87e74b0f79cdf1e3a","sha":"8a0752b447c2fcc1580afdc87e74b0f79cdf1e3a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/8a0752b447c2fcc1580afdc87e74b0f79cdf1e3a"}],"sha":"61e67654c80c36dff5a4ea8ecbe2998ee7df465a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/61e67654c80c36dff5a4ea8ecbe2998ee7df465a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13999850?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce","id":13999850,"login":"davidarce","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTk5ODUw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/8a0752b447c2fcc1580afdc87e74b0f79cdf1e3a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-03T14:40:29Z","email":"davidarce2915@gmail.com","name":"David Arce"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-03T14:40:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(sdd): cleanup — drop !-mkdir at skill load, move file-slicing to references/ (M7+M8) (#40)\n\n* refactor(sdd): drop double mkdir at skill load, move file-slicing rules to references/ (M7+M8)\n\nFinal cleanup pass for the audit umbrella (#33).\n\nM8 — drop the `!`-mkdir directive in sdd-orchestrator/SKILL.md\n\nThe line `!`mkdir -p .sdd/$1`` ran at skill-load time with whatever\ncwd the agent had. That was the original cause of the path bug fixed\nin #31: when cwd had drifted into a nested repo, `.sdd/{change}/`\nlanded in the wrong place. Post-#31 the canonical creation lives in\nREGISTRY.md step 3 with an absolute project path captured at\norchestrator start. Two creation paths is one too many — and the\n`!`-version is the wrong one. Drop it. The SKILL.md body now points\nto step 3 explicitly.\n\nM7 — move file-slicing rules out of sdd-explore/SKILL.md\n\nSlicing is conditional reference material — it only applies when\nthe exploration''s token budget is tight. The 10-line `## References:\nfile slicing` section in `sdd-explore/SKILL.md` was loaded on every\ninvocation regardless. Moved to `sdd-explore/references/file_slicing.md`\n(matching the existing `sdd-plan/references/` pattern); SKILL.md now\npoints at it via the inline link in the \"Mode priority\" bullet and a\nReferences-section pointer at the bottom.\n\nPer-file deltas:\n\n| File                                       | before | after | Δ    |\n|--------------------------------------------|-------:|------:|-----:|\n| sdd-orchestrator/SKILL.md                  |     41 |    39 |  -2  |\n| sdd-explore/SKILL.md                       |    127 |   116 | -11  |\n| sdd-explore/references/file_slicing.md     |   (new)|    28 | +28  |\n\nThe new references file is +28 lines but only loaded when needed; the\nSKILL.md (loaded every invocation) is 11 lines lighter. DevRune\nrenderer tests still pass — `references/` directories under skills\nare copied via `copySkillSubdirs` already, so the new file is\ninstalled transparently.\n\nCloses M7 + M8 of #33.\n\n* refactor(sdd): drop maintainer-facing cross-references in phase References sections\n\nAddress review comments on #40.\n\n1) sdd-orchestrator/SKILL.md — drop the explanatory tail about Step 3\n   of REGISTRY.md. The SKILL.md body just says \"Read ORCHESTRATOR.md\n   FIRST and COMPLETELY\"; the orchestrator''s own playbook is the\n   single source of truth and tells it what to do. REGISTRY is the\n   ambient-rules entry point (CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md), not something\n   the orchestrator consults from inside its skill body — pointing\n   \"(per REGISTRY.md)\" was confusing.\n\n2) Phase SKILL.md (explore / plan / implement / review) — drop the\n   \"Related SDD workflow skills: [sdd-...](...)\" links from each\n   References section. Reading another phase''s SKILL.md from inside\n   a phase agent is exactly the anti-pattern the audit flagged\n   (\"Reading SKILL.md files from other SDD phases — wastes context\n   tokens\"). The cross-references were maintainer-facing trivia\n   pretending to be a runtime navigation aid. Kept: shared contracts,\n   advisor pointers, and phase-specific reference material — those\n   are all useful at runtime.\n\n5 files, +5/-5.","tree":{"sha":"befbcb6c5ba1d0fa6a711e2cf01d9746fe220ba3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/trees/befbcb6c5ba1d0fa6a711e2cf01d9746fe220ba3"},"url":"https://api.github