-explore/references/file_slicing.md     |   (new)|    28 | +28  |\n\nThe new references file is +28 lines but only loaded when needed; the\nSKILL.md (loaded every invocation) is 11 lines lighter. DevRune\nrenderer tests still pass — `references/` directories under skills\nare copied via `copySkillSubdirs` already, so the new file is\ninstalled transparently.\n\nCloses M7 + M8 of #33.\n\n* refactor(sdd): drop maintainer-facing cross-references in phase References sections\n\nAddress review comments on #40.\n\n1) sdd-orchestrator/SKILL.md — drop the explanatory tail about Step 3\n   of REGISTRY.md. The SKILL.md body just says \"Read ORCHESTRATOR.md\n   FIRST and COMPLETELY\"; the orchestrator''s own playbook is the\n   single source of truth and tells it what to do. REGISTRY is the\n   ambient-rules entry point (CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md), not something\n   the orchestrator consults from inside its skill body — pointing\n   \"(per REGISTRY.md)\" was confusing.\n\n2) Phase SKILL.md (explore / plan / implement / review) — drop the\n   \"Related SDD workflow skills: [sdd-...](...)\" links from each\n   References section. Reading another phase''s SKILL.md from inside\n   a phase agent is exactly the anti-pattern the audit flagged\n   (\"Reading SKILL.md files from other SDD phases — wastes context\n   tokens\"). The cross-references were maintainer-facing trivia\n   pretending to be a runtime navigation aid. Kept: shared contracts,\n   advisor pointers, and phase-specific reference material — those\n   are all useful at runtime.\n\n5 files, +5/-5.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp915dCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKrAQAG8roxzgD2eh/PHJ29FnsfwZ\nwv4gTZS12rSlg9d3zbYB5rQDwtbM+Vrq+WCkHYDZBHze0W+ZK3ETCfwssCZGfNLB\n9uG4iO3XlCH9/aT5Ye2c5QwnviG/TGFXxmm/zw1st/KeikP9+DQ2YCZ6sB0WSy2L\nQhYuQoU6hT7ZUbPQGaG5Q/qcuPyELUzzzzB5rVvqCKVcOXcfLKfDEoorfNzTKvgA\nRHtrEkmWhThupOBc2ZBOfzH8pLzAMf3lexMLUl+Q17yFg8ihYoQnHFSsYfAPZ+8Z\ns0NKFFPoKMKE90vDfwffT1NtzzDli5kqAbsWziiiz