5edbd12f4b0ced23fff7193efe41e539/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-03T14:27:33Z","email":"davidarce2915@gmail.com","name":"David Arce"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-03T14:27:33Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(sdd): slim launch templates — keep dynamic context only (M5) (#38)\n\n* refactor(sdd): slim launch templates — drop operational contract, keep dynamic context only (M5)\n\nEvery launch prompt repeated the same operational-contract blocks\n(WAVE-SCOPE DISCIPLINE, QUALITY GATE, PERSISTENCE, ENVELOPE) inline,\neven though those rules already live canonically in:\n\n- `sdd-{phase}/SKILL.md` (per-phase Persistence + Return Envelope +\n  Self-Check sections — slimmed in #36)\n- `_shared/persistence-contract.md` (Phase Artifact Save Convention,\n  General Knowledge Persistence, Engram Availability Guard, Two-Step\n  Recovery)\n- `_shared/envelope-contract.md` (envelope format + last-output rule)\n\nThe orchestrator generates many launch prompts per workflow (one per\nimplement batch, plus explore/plan/review/crit-re-entry). Repeating\n30–40 lines of static contract per prompt drained the orchestrator''s\ncontext window with content the sub-agent already loads from its\nSKILL.md at start.\n\nStrip the redundant blocks across all 4 launch-template variants\n(base / claude / copilot / opencode) plus the Plan-Guidance re-entry\nin advisor-templates.md. Launch prompts now carry **dynamic context\nonly**: project path, change name, artifact list, batch directive,\noptional BACKGROUND MODE warning when run_in_background is true.\n\nPer-variant retention rules (unchanged):\n- Claude: no skill-load directive (auto-loads via skills frontmatter)\n- Copilot: no skill-load directive (.agent.md inlines SKILL.md)\n- OpenCode: keep \"read SKILL.md first\" directive (1-line opencode.json\n  prompts have no native pre-load)\n- base (codex / factory): keep Skill() with file-fallback\n\nCounts:\n\n| File                          | before | after | Δ      |\n|-------------------------------|-------:|------:|-------:|\n| launch-templates.md           |    220 |   160 | -60    |\n| launch-templates.claude.md    |    234 |   139 | -95    |\n| launch-templates.copilot.md   |    190 |   121 | -69    |\n| launch-templates.opencode.md  |    198 |   121 | -77    |\n| advisor-templates.md          |    166 |   160 | -6     |\n| **total (5 files)**           | **1008** | **701** | **-307** |\n\nDevRune renderer tests still pass — none of those tests assert on the\nspecific launch-template text we removed.\n\nCloses M5 of #33.\n\n* refactor(sdd): drop maintainer-facing prose and BACKGROUND MODE warning from launch templates\n\nAddress review comments on #38. Three pieces of bloat that didn''t\nserve the agent:\n\n1. Explanatory paragraph at the top of each variant\n   (\"Launch prompts carry dynamic context only...\"). Maintainer-\n   facing trivia — the slim templates speak for themselves and the\n   SYNC comment is enough for editors.\n\n2. Per-variant skill-loading note (\"Sub-agents auto-load via skills\n   frontmatter\", \"agent file IS the system prompt\", \"directive must\n   be retained\"). The agent doesn''t read this file as instruction;\n   maintainers don''t need three sentences to understand that the\n   prompts have a load directive in some variants and not in others\n   — the prompts themselves show that.\n\n3. BACKGROUND MODE warning in parallel-batch prompts (Claude variant\n   only — base also had a residual copy from earlier drafts).\n   `sdd-implement/SKILL.md` does not include `AskUserQuestion` in\n   `allowed-tools`, so the sub-agent literally cannot interact with\n   the user regardless of background/foreground. The warning was\n   defensive guidance against an action the runtime already prevents.\n\nSYNC comments at the top of each variant are kept as one-liners —\nthey are the only maintainer-facing note that earns its keep.\n\n4 files, +6/-38, applied uniformly across base / claude / copilot /\nopencode (the user noted on Claude but flagged \"may apply to all\nvariants\").","tree":{"sha":"0a3e15911e47bd64f1987600d1bf0c1b96846c48","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/trees/0a3e15911e47bd64f1987600d1bf0c1b96846c48"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/commits/367f881c5edbd12f4b0ced23fff7193efe41e539","verification":{"payload":"tree 0a3e15911e47bd64f1987600d1bf0c1b96846c48\nparent 82114ba598bcf3bb10db2bf215993ec0c03b6152\nauthor David Arce <davidarce2915@gmail.com> 1777818453 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777818453 +0200\n\nrefactor(sdd): slim launch templates — keep dynamic context only (M5) (#38)\n\n* refactor(sdd): slim launch templates — drop operational contract, keep dynamic context only (M5)\n\nEvery launch prompt repeated the same operational-contract blocks\n(WAVE-SCOPE DISCIPLINE, QUALITY GATE, PERSISTENCE, ENVELOPE) inline,\neven though those rules already live canonically in:\n\n- `sdd-{phase}/SKILL.md` (per-phase Persistence + Return Envelope +\n  Self-Check sections — slimmed in #36)\n- `_shared/persistence-contract.md` (Phase Artifact Save Convention,\n  General Knowledge Persistence, Engram Availability Guard, Two-Step\n  Recovery)\n- `_shared/envelope-contract.md` (envelope format + last-output rule)\n\nThe orchestrator generates many launch prompts per workflow (one per\nimplement batch, plus explore/plan/review/crit-re-entry). Repeating\n30–40 lines of static contract per prompt drained the orchestrator''s\ncontext window with content the sub-agent already loads from its\nSKILL.md at start.\n\nStrip the redundant blocks across all 4 launch-template variants\n(base / claude / copilot / opencode) plus the Plan-Guidance re-entry\nin advisor-templates.md. Launch prompts now carry **dynamic context\nonly**: project path, change name, artifact list, batch directive,\noptional BACKGROUND MODE warning when run_in_background is true.\n\nPer-variant retention rules (unchanged):\n- Claude: no skill-load directive (auto-loads via skills frontmatter)\n- Copilot: no skill-load directive (.agent.md inlines SKILL.md)\n- OpenCode: keep \"read SKILL.md first\" directive (1-line opencode.json\n  prompts have no native pre-load)\n- base (codex / factory): keep Skill() with file-fallback\n\nCounts:\n\n| File                          | before | after | Δ      |\n|-------------------------------|-------:|------:|-------:|\n| launch-templates.md           |    220 |   160 | -60    |\n| launch-templates.claude.md    |    234 |   139 | -95    |\n| launch-templates.copilot.md   |    190 |   121 | -69    |\n| launch-templates.opencode.md  |    198 |   121 | -77    |\n| advisor-templates.md          |    166 |   160 | -6     |\n| **total (5 files)**           | **1008** | **701** | **-307** |\n\nDevRune renderer tests still pass — none of those tests assert on the\nspecific launch-template text we removed.\n\nCloses M5 of #33.\n\n* refactor(sdd): drop maintainer-facing prose and BACKGROUND MODE warning from launch templates\n\nAddress review comments on #38. Three pieces of bloat that didn''t\nserve the agent:\n\n1. Explanatory paragraph at the top of each variant\n   (\"Launch prompts carry dynamic context only...\"). Maintainer-\n   facing trivia — the slim templates speak for themselves and the\n   SYNC comment is enough for editors.\n\n2. Per-variant skill-loading note (\"Sub-agents auto-load via skills\n   frontmatter\", \"agent file IS the system prompt\", \"directive must\n   be retained\"). The agent doesn''t read this file as instruction;\n   maintainers don''t need three sentences to understand that the\n   prompts have a load directive in some variants and not in others\n   — the prompts themselves show that.\n\n3. BACKGROUND MODE warning in parallel-batch prompts (Claude variant\n   only — base also had a residual copy from earlier drafts).\n   `sdd-implement/SKILL.md` does not include `AskUserQuestion` in\n   `allowed-tools`, so the sub-agent literally cannot interact with\n   the user regardless of background/foreground. The warning was\n   defensive guidance against an action the runtime already prevents.\n\nSYNC comments at the top of each variant are kept as one-liners —\nthey are the only maintainer-facing note that earns its keep.\n\n4 files, +6/-38, applied uniformly across base / claude / copilot /\nopencode (the user noted on Claude but flagged \"may apply to all\nvariants\").","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp91tVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+PkQAD7Je4npCfHWRfyPjyEG16TP\nlcpvn4tBw+7OnTDPWl/YPLvg3Omg/AfanGSDYKcacASSPoHZFsBg9O9pC4tz9akF\nUSCPlZi5WOojX/a0EbcN4ENUW0SavREkVW6On9Jnsq+W4guxFPjKvk4VcakbZOLk\nVuPEwUmqtb7LkeH63cJfXpXFumczMewR020eNXpnrR3+NSa/E9B0h1WxA4C/ugRj\nAFdf3jCboDlTx6W5+n4lZOR39HjCp6IFkXDpCKUFD6U8IeF/jBIiA6qybK0dPGQH\nJCRuNNDRy/Nap42rw6bdOYQGdnBmQexr1M1qTkxKDQuJHada1UjMgkKTC+xNS7lC\n5jMuGBWAUAfBhkkX2DBvz1WspUaFxr2DvIEttJTw/hQG4Zl6IsvfUhYXVKuJEJKZ\nX4rC3x2mKKn+N6+7rZEyvvFSAgeHRywRFEu0lpXFOPuNB8YWoBXwzECVCuFHcBKq\n8ips3fNnjqKQHmlzQnmKpRomGyQZH14k+aTxXpNj75wp7XnNoSzVE/q6mrlhhTFQ\nsWLRlaTVBP/4NDuXv4/ZpVAEMcX7+iJJgKPtzly84ri7lb/dP24mLPgdsvw9xLw9\nNzF348FKj+UV5GbHOMz/V1ZUN+sIh4nKIN6MVzDsHGNY8bKZnWNwW5U/jDcjbJ+G\nijo+n4tkhtHGeDnHTtm2\n=9hF/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-05-03T14:27:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/us