3f54bd91c986f9c5","node_id":"C_kwDORwxuadoAKGY4NjcyNzc5NjRkMGJlNDRiMzg4YWZhOTNmNTRiZDkxYzk4NmY5YzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commit/c5d94c9c5878001e843babc64b6d29c511071907","sha":"c5d94c9c5878001e843babc64b6d29c511071907","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/c5d94c9c5878001e843babc64b6d29c511071907"}],"sha":"f867277964d0be44b388afa93f54bd91c986f9c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/f867277964d0be44b388afa93f54bd91c986f9c5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13999850?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/davidarce","id":13999850,"login":"davidarce","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzOTk5ODUw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/c5d94c9c5878001e843babc64b6d29c511071907/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T18:50:04Z","email":"davidarce2915@gmail.com","name":"David Arce"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T18:50:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(sdd): hard role invariant for the orchestrator + post-compaction re-assertion (M1+M2) (#34)\n\nThe \"delegate-only\" contract was enunciated weakly across the SDD\nworkflow: a sentence in REGISTRY.md, a buried line in recovery.md,\nand a generic \"Load Skill(sdd-orchestrator)\" message in the post-\ncompaction hook. After context compaction, the orchestrator was\nrecovering state and re-loading the skill, but starting to edit code\ndirectly — losing the delegate role.\n\nTriple-defense the contract:\n\n1) Add a \"Role Invariant\" block at the top of every ORCHESTRATOR\n   variant (base, claude, copilot, opencode), named per the variant''s\n   invocation mechanism (Task / Agent / @<sub-agent>). The block\n   states what the orchestrator does (delegate, AskUserQuestion,\n   mkdir, Bash(crit ...)) and what it explicitly does NOT (Edit/Write\n   source files, build/test/lint, git commit/push, Skill(\"sdd-{phase}\")).\n\n2) Add the same block to REGISTRY.md and REGISTRY.claude.md (loaded\n   into the agent''s ambient rules / catalog file), so it survives\n   context compaction even when the orchestrator skill is not\n   currently loaded.\n\n3) Promote the existing one-line role mention in _shared/recovery.md\n   into the canonical block, placed BEFORE the recovery steps so the\n   orchestrator re-asserts the role before resuming.\n\n4) Replace the generic \"Load Skill\" message in the post-compaction\n   hooks with the role invariant verbatim:\n   - hooks/sdd-session-compact.sh (Claude SessionStart(compact) hook)\n   - plugins/sdd-compaction.ts (OpenCode experimental.session.compacting)\n   Both now emit the full Role Invariant block as part of recovered\n   context, then the recovery steps.\n\nCloses M1 + M2 of #33.","tree":{"sha":"1fcce4e98da356fb3bdf21ef3528a5bac2b8b7ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/trees/1fcce4e98da356fb3bdf21ef3528a5bac2b8b7ee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/commits/c5d94c9c5878001e843babc64b6d29c511071907","verification":{"payload":"tree 1fcce4e98da356fb3bdf21ef3528a5bac2b8b7ee\nparent 380ad14a0288c192d96a5b1a0557f459f0456ae0\nauthor David Arce <davidarce2915@gmail.com> 1777661404 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777661404 +0200\n\nfeat(sdd): hard role invariant for the orchestrator + post-compaction re-assertion (M1+M2) (#34)\n\nThe \"delegate-only\" contract was enunciated weakly across the SDD\nworkflow: a sentence in REGISTRY.md, a buried line in recovery.md,\nand a generic \"Load Skill(sdd-orchestrator)\" message in the post-\ncompaction hook. After context compaction, the orchestrator was\nrecovering state and re-loading the skill, but starting to edit code\ndirectly — losing the delegate role.\n\nTriple-defense the contract:\n\n1) Add a \"Role Invariant\" block at the top of every ORCHESTRATOR\n   variant (base, claude, copilot, opencode), named per the variant''s\n   invocation mechanism (Task / Agent / @<sub-agent>). The block\n   states what the orchestrator does (delegate, AskUserQuestion,\n   mkdir, Bash(crit ...)) and what it explicitly does NOT (Edit/Write\n   source files, build/test/lint, git commit/push, Skill(\"sdd-{phase}\")).\n\n2) Add the same block to REGISTRY.md and REGISTRY.claude.md (loaded\n   into the agent''s ambient rules / catalog file), so it survives\n   context compaction even when the orchestrator skill is not\n   currently loaded.\n\n3) Promote the existing one-line role mention in _shared/recovery.md\n   into the canonical block, placed BEFORE the recovery steps so the\n   orchestrator re-asserts the role before resuming.\n\n4) Replace the generic \"Load Skill\" message in the post-compaction\n   hooks with the role invariant verbatim:\n   - hooks/sdd-session-compact.sh (Claude SessionStart(compact) hook)\n   - plugins/sdd-compaction.ts (OpenCode experimental.session.compacting)\n   Both now emit the full Role Invariant block as part of recovered\n   context, then the recovery steps.\n\nCloses M1 + M2 of #33.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCA