epos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/587580bb340df01f96685f2d6194af40b138f2b4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T17:24:11Z","email":"davidarce2915@gmail.com","name":"David Arce"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T17:24:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(sdd): anchor artifact paths to {project path} and cite SKILL.md via {SKILLS_PATH} (#31)\n\nTwo related path bugs in the SDD workflow templates:\n\n1) `.sdd/{change}/` artifacts ended up inside nested repos when the\n   workspace contained more than one git repo. Root cause: REGISTRY.md\n   told the orchestrator to use a RELATIVE `mkdir -p .sdd/{change}`,\n   and every sub-agent launch prompt repeated the relative form for\n   `Artifact directory:`, `Primary: always write to ...`, and\n   `Previous artifacts:`. A sub-agent running with cwd in a nested\n   repo would then resolve `.sdd/...` against that nested cwd.\n\n   Templates now use `{project path}/.sdd/{change-name}/` (absolute)\n   for every artifact reference. `{project path}` is already the\n   absolute path the orchestrator injects into each launch prompt, so\n   the substitution side requires nothing new.\n\n2) OpenCode launch prompts cited SKILL.md at\n   `{WORKFLOW_DIR}/sdd-{phase}/SKILL.md`, which DevRune resolves to\n   `<workspace>/sdd-orchestrator/sdd-{phase}/SKILL.md` — a path that\n   does not exist. SKILL.md actually lives under `{SKILLS_PATH}` (the\n   skill install root, which DevRune''s renderer resolves to e.g.\n   `<workspace>/.agents/skills/sdd-{phase}/SKILL.md`).\n\n   All three SKILL.md citations in launch-templates.opencode.md now\n   use `{SKILLS_PATH}/sdd-{phase}/SKILL.md`.\n\nCloses #29","tree":{"sha":"cca9d0b99595ddb61142ba31e18ac077ed517db4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/trees/cca9d0b99595ddb61142ba31e18ac077ed517db4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/commits/587580bb340df01f96685f2d6194af40b138f2b4","verification":{"payload":"tree cca9d0b99595ddb61142ba31e18ac077ed517db4\nparent 9de92a3af2f580b692050a4afb4e3bb76d7463e5\nauthor David Arce <davidarce2915@gmail.com> 1777656251 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777656251 +0200\n\nfix(sdd): anchor artifact paths to {project path} and cite SKILL.md via {SKILLS_PATH} (#31)\n\nTwo related path bugs in the SDD workflow templates:\n\n1) `.sdd/{change}/` artifacts ended up inside nested repos when the\n   workspace contained more than one git repo. Root cause: REGISTRY.md\n   told the orchestrator to use a RELATIVE `mkdir -p .sdd/{change}`,\n   and every sub-agent launch prompt repeated the relative form for\n   `Artifact directory:`, `Primary: always write to ...`, and\n   `Previous artifacts:`. A sub-agent running with cwd in a nested\n   repo would then resolve `.sdd/...` against that nested cwd.\n\n   Templates now use `{project path}/.sdd/{change-name}/` (absolute)\n   for every artifact reference. `{project path}` is already the\n   absolute path the orchestrator injects into each launch prompt, so\n   the substitution side requires nothing new.\n\n2) OpenCode launch prompts cited SKILL.md at\n   `{WORKFLOW_DIR}/sdd-{phase}/SKILL.md`, which DevRune resolves to\n   `<workspace>/sdd-orchestrator/sdd-{phase}/SKILL.md` — a path that\n   does not exist. SKILL.md actually lives under `{SKILLS_PATH}` (the\n   skill install root, which DevRune''s renderer resolves to e.g.\n   `<workspace>/.agents/skills/sdd-{phase}/SKILL.md`).\n\n   All three SKILL.md citations in launch-templates.opencode.md now\n   use `{SKILLS_PATH}/sdd-{phase}/SKILL.md`.\n\nCloses #29","reason":"valid","signature":"-----B