ps://api.github.com/users/davidarce/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davidarce","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/commits/9c59a88c90e9306d0954f464c1adc4ce5cfc3a5e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T17:00:03Z","email":"davidarce2915@gmail.com","name":"David Arce"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T17:00:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(sdd): auto-launch implement after Crit plan approval (#23)\n\nAfter the plan phase completes Crit human review with no unresolved\ncomments, auto-launch the implement phase instead of asking\n\"Continue to implement / Review artifacts / Abort\". The human already\napproved the plan inline via Crit, so the prompt was redundant friction\non every plan→implement transition.\n\nChanges (applied to all four orchestrator variants — codex/factory,\nclaude, copilot, opencode):\n\n- Post-Phase step 7: new bullet for `plan ok` post-crit-approved →\n  auto-launch implement.\n- Crit confirmation guard: when `crit_completed: true`, auto-launch\n  implement directly. The guard now mainly serves compaction recovery.\n- Crit Plan Review Protocol: the \"no unresolved comments\" branch sets\n  `crit_completed: true` in state.yaml and proceeds to step 7.\n- _shared/persistence-contract.md: document `crit_completed` in the\n  state.yaml schema. Previously read by the guard but never written\n  (latent bug).\n\nCloses #22","tree":{"sha":"7c2a3e1e96008690b7ccc4abf27e502c8060bbd2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/trees/7c2a3e1e96008690b7ccc4abf27e502c8060bbd2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/commits/9c59a88c90e9306d0954f464c1adc4ce5cfc3a5e","verification":{"payload":"tree 7c2a3e1e96008690b7ccc4abf27e502c8060bbd2\nparent 8d78c0fc3379ac462c52cbfe59eb009474bfdb75\nauthor David Arce <davidarce2915@gmail.com> 1777654803 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777654803 +0200\n\nfeat(sdd): auto-launch implement after Crit plan approval (#23)\n\nAfter the plan phase completes Crit human review with no unresolved\ncomments, auto-launch the implement phase instead of asking\n\"Continue to implement / Review artifacts / Abort\". The human already\napproved the plan inline via Crit, so the prompt was redundant friction\non every plan→implement transition.\n\nChanges (applied to all four orchestrator variants — codex/factory,\nclaude, copilot, opencode):\n\n- Post-Phase step 7: new bullet for `plan ok` post-crit-approved →\n  auto-launch implement.\n- Crit confirmation guard: when `crit_completed: true`, auto-launch\n  implement directly. The guard now mainly serves compaction recovery.\n- Crit Plan Review Protocol: the \"no unresolved comments\" branch sets\n  `crit_completed: true` in state.yaml and proceeds to step 7.\n- _shared/persistence-contract.md: document `crit_completed` in the\n  state.yaml schema. Previously read by the guard but never written\n  (latent bug).\n\nCloses #22","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp9NwTCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4uEQAF/U6jTWLkb2vMoDHeNhiqV8\nya131t6draiZf/tZP4Oq6T3Yi8Qoc401JB7MpgPK7OQyFxyKtwzo85hQHdXxAFLv\nK7DhqWuOaFrjq8ptYWj8o9/nlG9gIF222cWoZ9sQ2ngPKLFNgydX+YJVOj2jufni\nrFEQlp9i5auAAINpDVXkASY7WgpZcGG417DEKF58ZgQ12jCHealcr/m9nBsMkC8U\nG+R72G+Gtxin2z62ONxnYXdnvK6AZEPVWPA4Bn2AywwWeqPj7I7sZwuBwCRhihY2\nN742/t9Ab0p+JhPnpDqmY8fUF4OusUcaBaEBOwGNTB+jmNAWEhR15Pk7e3VIBjuC\nXM9BZnFdDWcsGrSkRtZgR0JsK3FfTtjOKj51Osok4ir1rOfB00s0E+mmMWppBgI3\neiOdY/1JXZb1NjLtqRCb0UIcXnXK0U7MMZ7a6NmnWtlhrMSR1bfIZGSLzwE3rEJC\nJKNXMfy94EmCXZH1PK7jj722jvHC/AQ4Lx7yw6suECE5eKp4KnQSF7ad3eTWDF8/\n9dz+zVjxzZh4zfkiwIy9H8PDEFJmN1D/R7Y86ZXomGysSPCAvnfQ7tm5f4y9x4Yd\n73uAUltXoRrsgTRMT4Ql