polished versions\nmaintained in lib-purchaseai/agents/shared/skills, bringing this catalog\nto parity. The previous files only had a process summary and a short\nrules list — a lot of the original authoring richness had been lost.\n\nWhat lands here:\n\n- git-commit: pre-resolved dynamic context (branch/status/diff/log),\n  JIRA-ID extraction from branch names + MCP lookup, 9-step workflow\n  covering type detection, scope derivation, breaking-change detection,\n  description generation, and verification. New references/ (commit\n  patterns + examples), config.json for default_base_branch /\n  jira_project_prefix, and scripts/branch-to-jira.sh helper.\n\n- git-pull-request: platform auto-detection (GitHub gh / GitLab glab),\n  JIRA-driven PR template selection, 10-step workflow with draft-by-\n  default, title/body validation checklist. New references/ template\n  fill-out guide, config.json for platform override, and seven PR\n  templates under assets/templates/ (bug, feature, docs, refactor,\n  test, performance, security).\n\n- Both skills: broadened When to Invoke with intent-based matching in\n  English and Spanish plus indirect-cue detection, so paraphrases like\n  \"haz commit\" or \"si crea el pr\" route to the skill without the user\n  having to type a specific phrase. Frontmatter metadata exposes the\n  auto_invoke guidance for any tooling that reads it.\n\n- Both skills: set model to haiku since these are mechanical git/CLI\n  flows (diff parsing, branch regex, template rendering) that don''t\n  benefit from a heavier reasoning model.\n\nPreserve the existing gotchas.md on both skills (they capture a\ndifferent class of anti-patterns than the inline ## Gotchas in the new\nSKILL.md) and reference them explicitly from the skill body.","tree":{"sha":"b6267e4436764a84e1526a2c7bb61adfcf67b588","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce/devrune-starter-catalog/git/trees/b6267e4436764a84e1526a2c7bb61adfcf67b588"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/davidarce