i.github.com/users/gmocontreras","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatiosSpa/matios-ui-framework/commits/ebf29fe790c59b1d93c9a09539c0207de724bfd9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T23:55:03Z","email":"25290231+gmocontreras@users.noreply.github.com","name":"GUILLERMO CONTRERAS"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T23:55:03Z","email":"25290231+gmocontreras@users.noreply.github.com","name":"GUILLERMO CONTRERAS"},"message":"feat(icons): accept both ''user'' and ''mts-icon-user'' in class-based icon configs\n\nMTS.Icon.get() already tolerates both the plain name and the mts-icon- prefixed\nform, but the two components that build the icon as a CSS class (Menu, PanelDropdown)\nonly worked with the prefixed form — ''user'' produced class=\"mts-icon user\", which\ninitAll() never matched, so no icon rendered. Normalized the class the same way get()\ndoes (prefix it when missing), so either form works everywhere. Menu''s overflowIcon\nflows through the same path; SideNav/Topbar use Menu, so they''re covered too.","tree":{"sha":"efba5290ff133284412b6261e44cbbf9f9a47aa5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatiosSpa/matios-ui-framework/git/trees/efba5290ff133284412b6261e44cbbf9f9a47aa5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/MatiosSpa/matios-ui-framework/git/commits/ebf29fe790c59b1d93c9a09539c0207de724bfd9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25290231?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmocontreras/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmocontreras/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmocontreras/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gmocontreras/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/gmocontreras","id":25290231,"login":"gmocontreras","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MjkwMjMx","