ptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AuraBootTeam/auraboot/commits/c8c1dfd83e19a9a2b928a831f5948ec59cc83485/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T03:55:24Z","email":"216647+vavi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"diqi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T03:55:24Z","email":"216647+vavi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"diqi"},"message":"Materialize imported codes onto wildcard roles so list consumers see them\n\nThe permission-check honor for the ''*'' wildcard fixes interceptor paths,\nbut sidebar menus and permission matrices resolve concrete role_permission\nrows through list joins, so menus registered by plugin imports stayed\ninvisible to the tenant admin (the CI nightly''s dashboard-management\nnavigation failed on exactly this). After a plugin import registers\npermissions and capability families, a binder now materializes every\nregistered code onto the roles holding the wildcard grant in that tenant,\nskipping codes owned by plugins imported later (those bind on their own\nimport) and evicting the authorization caches. Fail-closed tests cover\nmaterialization and the not-yet-registered skip.","tree":{"sha":"fafa36164d6c61360584b8550a959c60e08f1a45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AuraBootTeam/auraboot/git/trees/fafa36164d6c61360584b8550a959c60e08f1a45"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AuraBootTeam/auraboot/git/commits/c8c1dfd83e19a9a2b928a831f5948ec59cc83485","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216647?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vavi","id":216647,"login":"vavi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjY0Nw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AuraBootTeam/auraboot/commit/c8c1dfd83e19a9a2b928a831f5948ec59cc83485","node_id":"C_kwDORxGGitoAKGM4YzFkZmQ4M2UxOWE5YTJiOTI4YTgzMWY1OTQ4ZWM1OWNjODM0ODU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AuraBootTeam/auraboot/commit/ebf272c39be922924fabf86a15e0a88b7d51e8d3","sha":"ebf272c39be922924fabf86a15e0a88b7d51e8d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AuraBootTeam/auraboot/commits/ebf272c39be922924fabf86a15e0a88b7d51e8d3"}],"sha":"c8c1dfd83e19a9a2b928a831f5948ec59cc83485","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AuraBootTeam/auraboot/commits/c8c1dfd83e19a9a2b928a831f5948ec59cc83485"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216647?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vavi","id":216647,"login":"vavi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjY0Nw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AuraBootTeam/auraboot/commits/8b555c56f44e93c0d574e35575f4031b6afb5cb6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T03:22:04Z","email":"216647+vavi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"diqi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T03:22:04Z","email":"216647+vavi@users.noreply.github.com","name":"diqi"},"message":"fix(automation): keep trigger fan-out alive on context-less worker threads\n\nRecord-trigger fan-out (onRecordCreate/onRecordUpdate/onFieldChange/\nonStateChange/onBpmEvent/onExternalEvent) runs on eventTaskExecutor\nworker threads. When the submitting thread carries no MetaContext —\nexternal-event consumers, BPM action workers, scheduler paths — the\ntenant-line interceptor threw \"MetaContext not initialized for current\nthread\" inside the first mapper query and the whole automation\nevaluation was lost to SimpleAsyncUncaughtExceptionHandler.\n\nObserved on the numnan multi-tenant acceptance domain (2026-10-07,\ncanary closure run): every record write routed through the external-\nevent/BPM action path produced the failure, so tenant automations\nsilently never fired in non-dev deployments.\n\nThe fan-out now resolves automations through findAutomationsForTrigger:\nwith a live MetaContext the behavior is byte-identical (tenant-filtered\nquery); without one it runs the same query under\nMetaContext.runWithoutTenantFilter — the event payload carries no\ntenant, so discovering the model''s enabled automations across tenants\nis the only correct semantic, and each match still executes under its\nown automation''s tenant scope via executeAutomation''s existing\nestablish-or-fallback (same doctrine the external-event path already\nuses).\n\nUnit tests cover both branches.","tree":{"sha":"ff130e64ba9d8fb90291690b67dda62496e79f25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AuraBootTeam/auraboot/git/trees/ff130e64ba9d8fb90291690b67dda62496e79f25"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AuraBootTeam/auraboot/git/commits/8b555c56f44e93c0d574e35575f4031b6afb5cb6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216647?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vavi","id":216647,"login":"vavi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjY0Nw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AuraBootTeam/auraboot/commit/8b555c56f44e93c0d574e35575f4031b6afb5cb6","node_id":"C_kwDORxGGitoAKDhiNTU1YzU2ZjQ0ZTkzYzBkNTc0ZTM1NTc1ZjQwMzFiNmFmYjVjYjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AuraBootTeam/auraboot/commit/ca1b1e846d77a637cbdf264d7944da1e8aae1d95","sha":"ca1b1e846d77a637cbdf264d7944da1e8aae1d95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AuraBootTeam/auraboot/commits/ca1b1e846d77a637cbdf264d7944da1e8aae1d95"}],"sha":"8b555c56f44e93c0d574e35575f4031b6afb5cb6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AuraBootTeam/auraboot/commits/8b555c56f44e93c0d574e35575f4031b6afb5cb6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/216647?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/vavi","id":216647,"login":"vavi","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjY0Nw==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vavi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AuraBootTeam/auraboot/commits/ca1b1e846d77a637cbdf264d7944da1e8aae1d95/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T02:44:05Z","email":"ghjapple@163.com","name":"vavi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T02:44:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(plugin): bind freshly imported plugin permissions to tenant_admin (#2229)\n\nCommit 63aac35a9 (#2157, capability-based explicit authorization) removed\nbindImportedPermissionsToTenantAdmin and switched import post-processing to\nregisterPermissions, which left fresh stacks with zero ab_role_permission\nrows for manifest-declared plugin permissions (bom.% family). The installing\ntenant_admin then 403s on plugin seed commands (bom:seed_defaults requires\nbom.rule.manage) and golden start reset fails.\n\nRestore the fresh-install bootstrap invariant while keeping #2157''s\nexplicit-authorization contract for synchronization: only permissions CREATED\nby this import are bound to the tenant''s tenant_admin role; UPDATE/SKIP\nre-imports never (re-)grant, so deliberately revoked grants are not restored.\nIdempotent (existing bindings skipped), per-permission best-effort, caches\nevicted only when a new binding was written.\n\nContract tests in PluginAccessResourceImporterTest cover: fresh creations bind\nto this tenant''s admin and invalidate caches; already-bound creations are not\nduplicated; UPDATE/SKIP re-imports never grant; missing tenant_admin does not\nfail the import.\n\nCo-authored-by: diqi <216647+vavi@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a00b60b81879a2c91e221faa03066a53946c47a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AuraBootTeam/auraboot/git/trees/a00b60b81879a2c91e221faa03066a53946c47a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AuraBootTeam/auraboot/git/commits/ca1b1e846d77a637cbdf264d7944da1e8aae1d95","verification":{"payload":"tree a00b60b81879a2c91e221faa03066a53946c47a1\nparent 57a8cac44b42217102e3ac8e87d322807f45a7ef\nauthor vavi <ghjapple@163.com> 1791341045 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791341045 +0800\n\nfix(plugin): bind freshly imported plugin permissions to tenant_admin (#2229)\n\nCommit 63aac35a9 (#2157, capability-based explicit authorization) removed\nbindImportedPermissionsToTenantAdmin and switched import post-processing to\nregisterPermissions, which left fresh stacks with zero ab_role_permission\nrows for manifest-declared plugin permissions (bom.% family). The installing\ntenant_admin then 403s on plugin seed commands (bom:seed_defaults requires\nbom.rule.manage) and golden start reset fails.\n\nRestore the fresh-install bootstrap invariant while keeping #2157''s\nexplicit-authorization contract for synchronization: only permissions CREATED\nby this import are bound to the tenant''s tenant_admin role; UPDATE/SKIP\nre-imports never (re-)grant, so deliberately revoked grants are not restored.\nIdempotent (existing bindings skipped), per-permission best-effort, caches\nevicted only when a new binding was written.\n\nContract tests in PluginAccessResourceImporterTest cover: fresh creations bind\nto this tenant''s admin and invalidate caches; already-bound creations are not\nduplicated; UPDATE/SKIP re-imports never grant; missing tenant_admin does not\nfail the import.\n\nCo-authored-by: diqi <216647+vavi@users.noreply.github.com>","