https://api.github.com/users/LingYuWings/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingYuWings/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingYuWings/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingYuWings/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LingYuWings","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LingYuWings/Radiflow-Player/commits/c8781c6d7c5c4e22a93806eb34d4d15b9c2c10e4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-28T15:31:21Z","email":"32763318+LingYuWings@users.noreply.github.com","name":"LingYu_Wings"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-28T15:31:21Z","email":"32763318+LingYuWings@users.noreply.github.com","name":"LingYu_Wings"},"message":"Add EQ UI and lyrics caching/database\n\nIntroduce a multi-band equalizer UI and integrate persistent lyric caching/storage. Adds a new EQView component and EQ state (bands, enabled flag, persistence) to the app, wired into the WebAudio graph via BiquadFilterNodes and persisted in preferences (storage version bumped). Update copy strings and exports (getEQCopy) and add UI controls to toggle/open the EQ overlay. On the server side, implement a lyrics subsystem: add /api/lyrics endpoint, support manual lyric files (.lrc/.yrc/.txt), introduce a sqlite-backed lyric_cache with migration from legacy JSON index files, and helper utilities for sanitizing, persisting and retrieving lyric payloads. Also update the useLyrics hook to accept fileUrl and query the new /api/lyrics endpoint.","tree":{"sha":"b9881146c3278e04680d018fac15f29197ce0fe8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LingYuWings/Radiflow-Player/git/trees/b9881146c3278e04680d018fac15f29197ce0fe8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/LingYuWings/Radiflow-Player/git/commits/c8781c6d7c5c4e22a93806eb34d4d15b9c2c10e4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"ava